window.GLOWSIS_2B = [{"id": 11, "title": "I came back on my way to the meetup place", "en": "약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요", "theme": "midway", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 11 · MIDWAY</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">11</div><div><h2>I came back on my way to the meetup place</h2><div class=\"en\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요 — Midway · -다가 “…and then” + 돌아오다 + past -았/었어요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · MEETUP DAY · MIDWAY</span>\n      <h3>약속 장소에서의 하루 — \"약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 멤버들이 <b>약속 장소</b>에서 만나기로 했어요. 그런데 <b>하준</b> 씨가 약속 장소에 <b>가다가</b> 생각났어요. \"아! 저는 핸드폰을 안 가져왔어요!\" 그래서 하준 씨는 집으로 <b>돌아왔어요</b>. 다시 가는 길에 조금 <b>늦었어요</b>. 다른 멤버들이 웃으며 말해요. \"하준 씨, 가다가 돌아왔어요? 우리 다 기다렸어요!\" 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today the members decided to meet at the <b>meetup place</b>. But <b>Hajun</b> suddenly remembered, <i>on his way there</i>: \"Ah! I didn't bring my phone!\" So Hajun <b>came back</b> home. Going there a second time made him a little <b>late</b>. The other members laugh, \"Hajun, you went and came back? We were all waiting!\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Notice the pattern: 가다가 돌아왔어요 — go, then come back on the way!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌍</span> Make promises &amp; name the meeting place (약속, 장소, 도중)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚶</span> -다가 (do one thing, then…) · 돌아오다 (come back) · 늦다 (be late)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📱</span> Use the past -았/었어요 to say \"I went &amp; came back\"</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — I Went &amp; Came Back!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 Outside the meetup place</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 오늘 약속 장소에서 만나요. 약속이 오후 두 시예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">We're meeting at the meetup place today. The appointment is at two PM!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저는 약속 장소에 가다가 아이스크림을 사고 싶어요. 🍦</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! On the way to the meetup place I want to buy some ice cream. 🍦</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">그런데 하준 씨는요? 하준 씨가 약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요. 전화도 안 받아요!</div><div class=\"gl\">But what about Hajun? He came back on the way to the meetup place. He's not answering calls either!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">그래요? 문자를 보냈어요. 아! 지금 문자가 왔어요. \"미안해요, 핸드폰을 안 가져왔어요!\" 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">Really? I sent a text. Oh! A text just came now. \"Sorry, I didn't bring my phone!\" 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">미안해요, 다들! 집에 가다가 생각나서 돌아왔어요. 그래서 조금 늦었어요. 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Sorry, everyone! I remembered on the way home, so I came back. That's why I'm a little late. 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-다가 — \"…and then / on the way, doing…\" (one action cut off by another)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-다가</b> to a verb stem to say you were doing one thing and then switched to (or were interrupted by) another. 가다 (go) → <b>가다가…</b> \"going, and then…\". 약속 장소에 가다가 = \"on the way to the meetup place\". 공부하다 (study) → <b>공부하다가…</b> \"while studying, then…\". The two actions are both real and in order.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 친구를 만났어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">On the way to the meetup place I met a friend.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">공부하다가 전화를 받았어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I was studying, then I answered the phone.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">길을 걷다가 비가 왔어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I was walking, and then it rained.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">돌아오다 — \"to come back / return\" (돌아 = back + 오다 = come)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>돌아오다</b> is the opposite of 가다 (go). 돌아오다 = 돌아 (back) + 오다 (come). Combine it with -다가 to say \"went part-way and came back\": 가다가 <b>돌아왔어요</b> = \"went (on the way) and came back\". 집으로 돌아와요 = \"come back home\", 다시 돌아왔어요 = \"came back again\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I came back on my way to the meetup place.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지금 집으로 돌아와요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm coming back home now.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 10분 후에 돌아올게요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'll come back in ten minutes.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-았/었어요 (past) — \"went / came back / was late\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To talk about a finished action, drop -아요/-어요 and add the past: 오다 → <b>왔어요</b> (came), 가다 → <b>갔어요</b> (went), 돌아오다 → 돌아와 + 었어요 = <b>돌아왔어요</b> (came back), 늦다 → <b>늦었어요</b> (was late). Combine with -다가 to describe what happened <i>on the way</i>: <b>가다가 돌아왔어요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I came back on my way to the meetup place. (돌아왔어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어제 친구를 만났어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I met a friend yesterday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 조금 늦었어요. 미안해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I was a little late. I'm sorry.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I came back on my way to the meetup place.\" (go part-way, then return)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">When an idol heads to a meetup but forgets something and turns around, Koreans slide a little \"on the way\" hook <b>-다가</b> onto the going verb, then land on the real action in the past: <b>가다가 돌아왔어요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-다가</b> means you started one action (가다 = going) and then switched to another — here coming back. So <span class=\"pt-ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요</span> = \"I was heading to the meetup place, and on the way I came back.\" Koreans say coming back with <b>돌아오다</b> (돌아 = back + 오다 = come), and the whole story is told in the past with <b>-았/었어요</b>:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">돌아왔어요</span> = came back (already did it).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">약속 장소에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to the meetup place <span class=\"t-sub\">(destination)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">약속 = promise/appointment, 장소 = place → <b>약속 장소</b> = the place you promise to meet. The particle <b>에</b> = \"to/toward\" the destination.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가다가</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">going… and then <span class=\"t-sub\">(가다 + -다가)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>-다가</b> = \"was doing one thing, and then…\". 가다 (go) → 가<b>다가</b> = \"on the way / while going\". Add 공부하다 (study) → 공부하<b>다가</b> = \"while studying\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">돌아왔어요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">came back <span class=\"t-sub\">(돌아오다 → 돌아왔어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">돌아오다 = come back. Past: 돌아와 + -았어요 → <b>돌아왔어요</b> \"came back\". So the full sentence says: I was going to the meeting place, and on the way I came back.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-다가 = \"…and then (in the middle)…\"</b> — it links two actions, and the second one often interrupts the first. The particle <b>에</b> marks where you're heading:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">약속 장소에 가다가</span> (on the way to the meetup place) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">돌아왔어요</span> (I came back). Idols say this all the time when they forget a fan letter or a phone on the way to a schedule!\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-어요 → plain present</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">약속 장소에 가요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I go to the meetup place.\" — a plain statement.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-았/었어요 → past</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">가다가 돌아왔어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I went (on the way) and came back.\" — already done.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>-다가</b> is the \"mid-journey switch\" — head somewhere (가다가), then <b>돌아오다</b> (come back), and you were <b>늦다</b> (late). Picture the path: ➡️ then 🔄 back. Practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">집에 가다가 돌아왔어요!</span> \"I went home and turned right back around!\"\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눈러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌍</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">약속과 만남<small>Appointment &amp; the meeting place · 약속 장소에서 만나요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a8_promise.webp\" alt=\"약속\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">약속</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yaksok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">promise / appointment</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_place.webp\" alt=\"장소\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('장소')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">장소</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jangso</div><div class=\"vw-en\">place / spot</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_midway.webp\" alt=\"도중\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('도중')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">도중</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dojung</div><div class=\"vw-en\">midway / on the way</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 약속이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘 약속이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have an appointment today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속 장소에서 만나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">약속 장소에서 만나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's meet at the meeting place.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가는 도중에 연락할게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가는 도중에 연락할게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll contact you on the way.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌍 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 약속 (appointment) + 장소 (place) = 약속 장소, the spot you promise to meet at. 도중 means “midway / on the way” — and going 도중 then coming back is exactly today's title!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚶</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">가는 길<small>Going and coming back · 가다가 돌아왔어요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b19_go.webp\" alt=\"가다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to go</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_comeback.webp\" alt=\"돌아오다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('돌아오다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">돌아오다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">doraoda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to come back</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_late.webp\" alt=\"늦다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('늦다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">늦다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">neutda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be late</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지금 집으로 돌아와요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지금 집으로 돌아와요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm coming back home now.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went on the way and came back.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조금 늦어요. 미안해요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">조금 늦어요. 미안해요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm a little late. Sorry!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚶 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 가다 (go) &amp; 돌아오다 (come back) are opposites. 늦다 (be late) is what happens when you go, come back, and go again!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📱</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">연락<small>Contacting each other · 전화해요, 문자를 보냐요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_phone.webp\" alt=\"전화\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('전화')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">전화</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeonhwa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">phone / phone call</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b11_text.webp\" alt=\"문자\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('문자')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">문자</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">munja</div><div class=\"vw-en\">text message</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저한테 전화해 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저한테 전화해 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please call me.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('문자를 보냈어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">문자를 보냈어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I sent a text message.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('문자가 왔요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">문자가 왔요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">A text message arrived.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📱 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 전화 (call) + 문자 (text) = how friends stay in touch. 받아요 means “answer / receive”, 보내요 means “send”, and 문자가 와요 = “a message comes.”</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-1] Reading — 약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 약속 장소에 가다가 돌아왔어요.</span> What did Jiwoo do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I arrived at the meeting place on time.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I went toward the meetup place, then came back on the way.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I will go to the meeting place tomorrow.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I stayed home all day and never went out.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">가다가</b> = “going / on the way, and then” (가다 + -다가). <b class=\"hl\">돌아왔어요</b> = 돌아오다 (come back) in the past. Together: “I went toward the meetup place, then on the way I came back.” Not “arrived”, not the future, and she clearly left the house.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-2] Grammar — -다가 (on the way)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the word that best fills the blank.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 약속 장소에 ______ 아이스크림을 샀어요.</span> Hajun bought ice cream ON THE WAY. Which form of 가다 fits?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 가다가<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 갔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 가고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가겠어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">“On the way” needs <b class=\"hl\">-다가</b>: 가다 + -다가 = <b class=\"hl\">가다가</b> “going, and then…” 갣어요 is past “went”, 가고 있어요 is “is going”, 가겠어요 is “will go” — none show the “while going” switch.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-3] Reading — 돌아왔어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 지금 집으로 돌아왔어요.</span> Seoyeon is saying she…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> left home to go out<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> is still waiting at the cafe<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> has come back home<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> called her manager<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">돌아오다</b> = “to come back / return”. Past form <b class=\"hl\">돌아왔어요</b> = “came back.” 집으로 = “to home.” So she has come back home — not left, not still out.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-4] Grammar — past of 돌아오다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct past form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 어제 약속 장소에 가다가 ______.</span> Which is the PAST of 돌아오다 meaning “came back”?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 돌아와요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 돌아올게요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 돌아오고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 돌아왔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Past tense: 돌아오다 stem 돌아와 + -았어요 = <b class=\"hl\">돌아왔어요</b> “came back.” 돌아와요 = present, 돌아올게요 = “I’ll come back”, 돌아오고 있어요 = “is coming back”.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-5] Reading — 가다가 전화했어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 약속 장소에 가다가 하준 씨한테 전화했어요.</span> What did Yuna do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She met Hajun at the meeting place.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> On the way to the meetup place she called Hajun.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Hajun came back home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She was late because of the phone call.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">가다가 = “on the way.” <b class=\"hl\">전화했어요</b> = past of 전화하다 (to call). So she called Hajun while on the way. Meeting, coming back, and being late are not said.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-6] Reading — 늦었어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 미안해요, 저는 늦었어요.</span> Hajun is saying…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> he is late<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> he came back early<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> he is lost<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> he bought the food<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">늦다</b> = “to be late.” Past <b class=\"hl\">늦었어요</b> = “was late.” With 미안해요 (sorry), Hajun is apologizing for being late — the natural follow-up to a comeback on the way.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-7] Grammar — building 가다가 + 만나다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that means “On the way to the meetup place I met a friend.”</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which Korean sentence matches the meaning?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 약속 장소에 만나서 친구를 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 가다가 약속 장소를 친구가 만났어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 약속 장소에 가다가 친구를 만났어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 친구를 가다가 만나서 약속 장소예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The natural order: place + 에 + 가다가 (“going to…”) + then the action <b class=\"hl\">친구를 만났어요</b> (met a friend). Only <b>가다가 친구를 만났어요</b> uses -다가 correctly.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-8] Grammar — past of 보내다 (send)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct past form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 아까 문자를 ______.</span> Jihoon SENT a text a moment ago. Which is correct?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 보내요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 보냈어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 보낼게요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 보내고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">아까 (a moment ago) tells us it’s finished → past. 보내다 (send) → <b class=\"hl\">보냈어요</b> “sent.” 보내요 = present, 보낼게요 = “I’ll send”, 보내고 있어요 = “am sending”.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-9] Reading — 가다가 돌아갔어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 하준 씨는 약속 장소에 가다가 집으로 돌아갔어요. 그래서 조금 늦었어요.</span> What happened to Hajun?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He went straight to the meeting place on time.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He never left his house.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Seoyeon called Hajun.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He went toward the place, came back home, and was a little late.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Piece it together: 가다가 = on the way, 돌아갣어요 = went back (past), 그래서 = so, 조금 늦었어요 = was a little late. Only ④ matches all parts.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-10] Reading — choosing the past form</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the word that fits the past sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">어제 저는 약속 장소에 가다가 ______.</span> (어제 = yesterday, so use the past.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b11q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 돌아왔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 돌아와요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 돌아올게요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b11q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 돌아오세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b11q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">어제 (yesterday) → a finished action → past <b class=\"hl\">돌아왔어요</b> “came back.” 돌아와요 = present, 돌아올게요 = “I’ll come back”, 돌아오세요 = polite “please come back.”</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Late? Text on the Way!</h3>\n    <p>In Korea, if an idol is going to be even a little late for a meetup, they call or text <i>on the way</i> (가는 도중에) to say so — that \"on the way, so I'll be late\" is exactly where -다가 shines. Turning around mid-journey to grab something forgotten is so common that 돌아오다 has its own friendly, everyday feel.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Try saying it: \"약속 장소에 가다가 조금 늦을 것 같아요. 미안해요!\" (On the way to the meetup place, I think I'll be a little late. Sorry!) — you'll sound just like Hajun apologizing to the members!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 12, "title": "What kind of person do you like?", "en": "사비나 씨는 어떤 사람을 좋아해요?", "theme": "liking-type", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 12 &middot; WHO DO YOU LIKE?</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">12</div><div><h2>What kind of person do you like?</h2><div class=\"en\">사비나 씨는 어떤 사람을 좋아해요? — Liking people · 어떤 + noun · -는/-(으)ㄴ person with personality &amp; appearance adjectives</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · WHO DO YOU LIKE?</span>\n      <h3>어떤 사람이 좋아요? — 사비나 씨의 이상형</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b>의 팬사인회 날이에요. 단골 팬 <b>사비나</b> 씨가 멤버들에게 물어요. \"저는 요즘 좋아하는 사람이 생겼어요. 여러분은 <b>어떤 사람</b>을 좋아해요?\" 멤버들은 재미있게 대답해요. \"저는 <b>친절한</b> 사람을 좋아해요!\", \"저는 <b>재미있는</b> 사람이요!\", \"전 <b>잘생긴</b> 분이요!\" 💙 팬들은 웃으며 서로의 이상형을 이야기해요.</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">It's <b>SAETBYEOL</b>'s fansign day. A regular fan, <b>Sabina</b>, asks the members: \"I have a crush these days. What <b>kind of person</b> do YOU like?\" The members answer playfully: \"I like <b>kind</b> people!\", \"I like <b>fun</b> people!\", \"I like someone <b>handsome</b>!\" 💙 The fans laugh and share their own ideal types.</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Ask WHAT KIND with 어떤, then describe people with -는 / -(으)ㄴ adjectives!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🙋</span> Ask &amp; say what kind of person you like</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✨</span> 어떤 + noun (what kind of …) · -는 / -(으)ㄴ 사람 (describing people)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💛</span> Personality &amp; appearance words: 착하다, 친절하다, 재미있다, 잘생기다</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — Ideal Types!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 Backstage before the fansign</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">사비나 씨가 우리에게 물었어요. \"어떤 사람을 좋아해요?\" 저는 친절한 사람을 좋아해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Sabina asked us, \"What kind of person do you like?\" I like kind people.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">전 재미있는 사람이요! 웃기고 활발한 사람을 좋아해요. 😄</div><div class=\"gl\">I like fun people! I like people who are funny and lively. 😄</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 성격이 좋은 사람이 좋아요. 잘생기거나 예쁜 것보다 중요해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I like people with a good personality. That's more important than being handsome or pretty.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요! 저는 노래를 잘하는 사람을 좋아해요. 🎤</div><div class=\"gl\">That's right! I like people who sing well. 🎤</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 조용한 사람보다는 착한 사람이 좋아요! 서로 힘이 되어 줄 수 있는 사람이요. 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Rather than quiet people, I like nice people — someone who can support me. 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">어떤 + noun — \"what kind of …\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>어떤</b> before a noun to ask <b>what kind / which sort of</b>: <b>어떤 사람</b> (what kind of person), <b>어떤 음악</b> (what kind of music), <b>어떤 영화</b> (what kind of movie). The answer usually adds a describing word: 친절한 사람 (a kind person) → 저는 <b>친절한</b> 사람을 좋아해요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떤 사람을 좋아해요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What kind of person do you like? (어떤 + 사람)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떤 음악을 좋아해요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What kind of music do you like?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떤 성격이 좋아요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What kind of personality is good?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-는 / -(으)ㄴ 사람 — describing a person (adnominal)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To describe a noun, a verb takes <b>-는</b> and an adjective takes <b>-(으)ㄴ</b> right before it: 노래를 <b>잘하는 사람</b> (a person who sings well), 친절<b>한 사람</b> (a kind person), 착<b>한 사람</b> (a nice person), 재미있<b>는 사람</b> (a fun person — 재미있다 → 재미있는). So 저는 <b>노래를 잘하는 친절한 사람</b>을 좋아해요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래를 잘하는 사람을 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I like people who sing well. (잘하다 → 잘하는)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">착한 사람이 좋아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Good-hearted people are nice. (착하다 → 착한)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">재미있는 사람과 이야기하고 싶어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to talk with fun people. (재미있다 → 재미있는)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">성격 &amp; 외모 adjectives for people</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Describe <b>personality</b> with: <b>착하다</b> (nice), <b>친절하다</b> (kind), <b>재미있다</b> (fun), <b>활발하다</b> (lively), <b>조용하다</b> (quiet). For <b>appearance</b>: <b>예쁘다</b> (pretty), <b>잘생기다</b> (handsome). Put them before 사람 or use the -해요/-이에요 form: 그 사람은 <b>정말 친절해요</b> (that person is really kind).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">그 사람은 정말 친절해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">That person is really kind. (친절하다 → 친절해요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 잘생긴 사람이 좋아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I like handsome people. (잘생기다 → 잘생긴)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유나는 성격이 활발해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yuna has a lively personality. (활발하다 → 활발해요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"사비나 씨는 어떤 사람을 좋아해요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">사비나 씨는 어떤 사람을 좋아해요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Sabina, what kind of person do you like?\" (asking about a type)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Idols get asked about \"types\" in interviews all the time. Instead of \"who,\" Korean uses <b>어떤 + noun</b> (\"what kind of\"). Then add a describing word like 친절한 / 잘생긴 to describe a whole person in one short phrase.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>어떤</b> = \"what kind of.\" You can never say <span class=\"pt-ko\">무엇 사람</span> — a noun needs <b>어떤</b> before it: <b>어떤 사람</b>. To describe, a verb takes <b>-는</b> (노래를 잘하<b>는</b> 사람) and an adjective takes <b>-(으)ㄴ</b> (친절<b>한</b> 사람, 잘생<b>긴</b> 사람). Stack them up:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">잘생기고 착한 사람</span> = \"a handsome and nice person.\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">사비나 씨는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">Sabina <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">사비나 = a person's name. <b>씨</b> = polite title after a name. <b>는</b> marks the topic — \"speaking of Sabina…\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어떤</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">what kind of <span class=\"t-sub\">(question word)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>어떤</b> sits directly before a noun to ask about a type: 어떤 사람, 어떤 음악, 어떤 영화.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">사람을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">person <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">사람 = person. The object marker <b>을</b> shows the person is the thing being liked: 사람<b>을</b> 좋아해요.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">좋아해요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to like <span class=\"t-sub\">(좋아하다 + -아/어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">좋아하다 = \"to like\" (a verb that takes an object). 좋아하다 → 좋아<b>해요</b>. Careful: 좋다 = \"to be good,\" 좋아하다 = \"to like\" — they are different!</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">어떤 = \"what kind of\"</b> — always follow it with a noun: <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떤 사람</span>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떤 팬</span>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떤 음악</span>. In casual talk idols also shorten a reply with a soft <b>-이요</b> tag: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 친절한 사람이요!</span> (\"Me? I like kind people!\").\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>교과서 · Textbook form</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어떤 사람을 좋아해요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"What kind of person do you like?\" — full, clear, polite.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>실제말 · Real speech</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어떤 스타일이 좋아요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"What (type/style) do you like?\" — shorter, casual, super common.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> wrong = <span class=\"pt-ko\">무엇 사람</span>, right = <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떤 사람</span>. Hear <b>-는</b> on a verb (잘하<b>는</b>) but <b>-(으)ㄴ</b> on an adjective (친절<b>한</b>) right before a person. Practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 노래를 잘하는 친절한 사람을 좋아해요!</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧸</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">성격<small>Personality</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_personality.webp\" alt=\"성격\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('성격')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">성격</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seonggyeok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">personality / character</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_nice.webp\" alt=\"착하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('착하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">착하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chakhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be nice / good-hearted</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_kind.webp\" alt=\"친절하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친절하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">친절하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chinjeolhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be kind</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you&rsquo;ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그 사람은 정말 착해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">그 사람은 정말 착해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">That person is really nice.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친절한 사람이 좋아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">친절한 사람이 좋아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Kind people are nice.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('성격이 정말 좋아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">성격이 정말 좋아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(She) has a really good personality.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🧸 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 성격 takes 이/가: 성격<b>이</b> 좋아요. 착하다 · 친절하다 drop 다 and add -ㄴ before 사람: 착<b>한</b> 사람, 친절<b>한</b> 사람. And 좋아하다 takes 을/를: 사람<b>을</b> 좋아해요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">☀️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">성격과 분위기<small>Temperament &amp; vibe</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_fun.webp\" alt=\"재미있다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('재미있다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">재미있다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jaemiitda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be fun / interesting</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_active.webp\" alt=\"활발하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('활발하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">활발하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hwalbalhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be active / lively</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_quiet.webp\" alt=\"조용하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조용하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">조용하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">joyonghada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be quiet</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you&rsquo;ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그 사람은 정말 재미있어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">그 사람은 정말 재미있어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">That person is really fun!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 조용한 사람이 좋아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 조용한 사람이 좋아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like quiet people.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('유나가 아주 활발해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">유나가 아주 활발해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Yuna is very lively.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">☀️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 재미있다 = to be fun, 활발하다 = energetic, 조용하다 = quiet. As describing words just add -ㄴ: 재미있<b>는</b> 사람, 활발<b>한</b> 사람, 조용<b>한</b> 사람.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">✨</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">외모<small>Appearance</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_pretty.webp\" alt=\"예쁘다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('예쁘다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">예쁘다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeppeuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be pretty</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_handsome.webp\" alt=\"잘생기다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('잘생기다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">잘생기다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jalsaenggida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be handsome</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you&rsquo;ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그분은 정말 예뻐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">그분은 정말 예뻐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">That person is really pretty.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 잘생긴 사람을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 잘생긴 사람을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like handsome people.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그는 참 잘생겼어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">그는 참 잘생겼어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">He is really handsome!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">✨ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 예쁘다 (pretty) is for girls / things, 잘생기다 (handsome) is for guys. Before 사람 they become 예쁜 사람, 잘생긴 사람 — adjectives just add -ㄴ.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-1] Reading — 어떤 사람이 좋아요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 친절하고 착한 사람이 좋아요.</span> What type of person does Seoyeon like?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> People who are kind and nice<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> People who are quiet and funny<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Only people who are very handsome<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> People who only study<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Cherish the two adjectives: <b class=\"hl\">친절한</b> (kind) and <b class=\"hl\">착한</b> (nice). Both describe personality and both take <b class=\"hl\">-ㄴ</b> before 사람. So she likes <b class=\"hl\">kind, nice</b> people — only ① matches.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-2] Reading — -는 사람</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 저는 노래를 잘하는 사람을 좋아해요.</span> Jihoon likes people who…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> are always late<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> can sing well<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> love to study Korean<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> are very tall<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <b class=\"hl\">잘하다</b> (to do well) becomes <b class=\"hl\">잘하는</b> before 사람. So <b class=\"hl\">노래를 잘하는 사람</b> = \"a person who sings well.\" The correct answer is ②.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-3] Grammar — 어떤 (what kind of)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct question word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Fill in the blank.<span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: ______ 음악을 좋아해요?</span> — \"What kind of music…?\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 무엇 (what)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어떤 (what kind of)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 누가 (who)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 어디 (where)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The noun <b class=\"hl\">음악</b> (music) needs <b class=\"hl\">어떤</b> in front to ask \"what kind of\": <b class=\"hl\">어떤 음악</b>. 무엇 means bare \"what,\" 누가 = who, 어디 = where — none work before a noun this way.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-4] Grammar — 친절한 (adjective + -ㄴ)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct describing form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Complete: 저는 <span class=\"pt-ko\">______ 사람을 좋아해요.</span> (use 친절하다)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 친절하는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 친절해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 친절하고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 친절한<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Adjectives put <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ</b> before a noun: 친절하다 → <b class=\"hl\">친절한</b> 사람. 친절하는 (wrong — that is the verb pattern), 친절해요 (plain ending), 친절하고 싶어요 (\"want to be kind\") are not the describing form.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-5] Reading — 잘생기다 (handsome)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 그 배우가 정말 잘생겼어요!</span> Hajun thinks the actor is…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> really quiet<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> really handsome<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> always late<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> very tall<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">잘생기다</b> = \"to be handsome,\" an appearance word used mostly for men. <b class=\"hl\">잘생겼어요</b> = \"(he) is handsome.\" The correct pick is ②.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-6] Grammar — make -는 사람</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate \"I like people who are fun.\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">재미있다</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 조용한 사람을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 재미있는 사람을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 예쁜 사람을 싫어해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 착한 사람을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">재미있다 is a special adjective: it becomes <b class=\"hl\">재미있는</b> (add -는, not -ㄴ!). So \"people who are fun\" = <b class=\"hl\">재미있는 사람</b> → ②. The others mix up quiet, pretty, and nice.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-7] Reading — 어떤 + personality</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what type Sabina likes.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">사비나: 저는 활발하고 재미있는 사람을 좋아해요.</span> Which type does Sabina like?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Lively and fun people<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Quiet and kind people<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Handsome but serious people<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Shy and loud people<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Combine <b class=\"hl\">활발하고</b> (and lively) with <b class=\"hl\">재미있는</b> (fun): she likes <b class=\"hl\">lively and fun</b> people — answer ①.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-8] Grammar — vocabulary match</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the word that means \"handsome\".</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which Korean word means <span class=\"pt-ko\">handsome</span>?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 예쁘다 (pretty)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 활발하다 (lively)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 조용하다 (quiet)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 잘생기다 (handsome)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">잘생기다 = <b class=\"hl\">handsome</b>, used for men. 예쁘다 = pretty, 활발하다 = lively, 조용하다 = quiet — the appearance word here is <b class=\"hl\">잘생기다</b> (④).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-9] Grammar — 조용한 사람 (a quiet person)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct phrase.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Make \"a quiet person\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용하다</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 조용해요 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 조용하고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 조용하는 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 조용한 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">조용하다 drops 다 and takes <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ</b>: <b class=\"hl\">조용한 사람</b> (a quiet person). 조용해요 사람 and 조용하는 사람 are wrong, and 조용하고 싶어요 = \"I want to be quiet.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-10] Reading — full sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Jiwoo is saying.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 잘생기고 착한 사람을 좋아해요. 그런데 너무 조용한 사람은 별로예요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b12q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She likes handsome, nice people, but not too-quiet ones.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She only likes very quiet people.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She likes tall, funny people.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b12q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She does not like anyone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b12q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Piece it together: <b class=\"hl\">잘생기고 착한 사람</b> = \"handsome and nice person,\" and <b class=\"hl\">너무 조용한 사람은 별로예요</b> = \"too-quiet people are not that great.\" Only ① matches both halves.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Ideal Types &amp; Idol Interviews</h3>\n    <p>In Korean interviews, idols get asked \"이상형이 어떻게 돼요?\" (What's your ideal type?) all the time. The natural reply is a quick 어떤 + describing phrase: 친절한 사람, 잘생긴 사람, 재미있는 사람. In everyday dating talk, young Koreans also say the real-life \"어떤 스타일이 좋아요?\" (what type do you like?) instead of the long textbook form.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Try saying: \"저는 재미있고 착한 사람을 좋아해요.\" (I like fun, nice people.) or ask a friend \"어떤 사람을 좋아해요?\" (What kind of person do you like?) — you'll sound like an idol in a live interview!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 13, "title": "Why don't we share the housework?", "en": "집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?", "theme": "housework", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 13 · HOUSEWORK</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">13</div><div><h2>Why don't we share the housework?</h2><div class=\"en\">집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때? — Housework · -는 게 어때? + 나누다/나눠서 + 집안일 하기</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · HOUSEWORK</span>\n      <h3>샛별의 집안일 나누기 — \"집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b>의 쉬는 날이에요. 그런데 집이 정말 더러워요. <b>설거지</b>도 있고 <b>빨래</b>도 많아요! 지우가 말해요. \"집안일이 너무 많아요. 우리 <b>집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때요?</b>\" 멤버들은 모두 좋아하며 청소, 요리, 쓰레기를 나눠서 해요. 🧹 함께 하니까 집안일이 금방 끝나요!</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today is <b>SAETBYEOL</b>'s day off. But the house is really messy — there are <b>dishes</b> to wash and so much <b>laundry</b>! Jiwoo says, \"There's so much housework. <b>Why don't we divide the housework and do it?</b>\" All the members happily split the cleaning, cooking, and trash. 🧹 When they do it together, the chores are done in no time!</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Make a kind suggestion with -는 게 어때? &amp; divide chores with 나눠서!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤝</span> Suggest an idea with -는 게 어때? (\"how about …ing?\")</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⚖️</span> Divide &amp; then … with 나누다 → 나눠서</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏠</span> Housework words: 청소, 빨래, 설거지, 요리, 쓰레기 &amp; more</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 13 — Let's Share the Housework!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏠 In the SAETBYEOL dorm living room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">우와, 오늘 집안일이 정말 많아요! 설거지도 있고 빨래도 있어요. 😅</div><div class=\"gl\">Wow, there's so much housework today! There are dishes and laundry. 😅</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 그럼 집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Okay! Then why don't we divide the housework and do it?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 빨래를 할게요. 설거지도 할 수 있어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I'll do the laundry. I can do the dishes too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">그러면 저는 청소를 해요. 요리는 하준이 하지 그래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Then I'll clean. Why doesn't Hajun do the cooking?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 요리는 제가 할게요! 그리고 쓰레기도 나눠서 버려요. 같이 하니까 힘들지 않아요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes, I'll cook! And let's divide the trash too. It's not hard when we do it together!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-는 게 어때? — \"how about …ing?\" (making a suggestion)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To suggest an idea softly, attach <b>-는 게 어때?</b> to a verb stem: 하다 → <b>하는 게 어때?</b> \"how about doing (it)?\" 빨래하다 → <b>빨래하는 게 어때?</b> \"how about we do laundry?\" It is a friendly way to ask someone's opinion before acting together.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">집안일을 나눠서 <b>하는 게 어때?</b></span><span class=\"gl\">Why don't we divide the housework and do it? (하다 + -는 게 어때)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 청소<b>하는 게 어때?</b></span><span class=\"gl\">How about we clean together?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 빨래<b>하는 게 어때?</b></span><span class=\"gl\">How about doing the laundry today?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">나누다 → 나눠서 — \"divide (it) &amp; then …\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>나누다</b> = to share / divide. Conjugated as <b>나눠서</b> (나누어서), the <b>-아/어서</b> ending means \"do this, then…\" So <b>집안일을 나눠서 해요</b> = \"divide the chores, then do them.\" It turns one big job into small parts everyone can handle.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">집안일을 <b>나눠서</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We divide the chores, then do them. (나누다 → 나눠서)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">설거지와 청소를 <b>나눠서</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We split the dishes and cleaning, then do them.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 요리를 하고 동생은 쓰레기를 버려요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I cook and my brother takes out the trash. (we shared it)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">집안일 하기 — housework vocabulary &amp; actions</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">For each chore Koreans pair the noun with a \"do\" verb: <b>청소를 하다</b> (do the cleaning), <b>빨래를 하다</b> (do the laundry), <b>설거지를 하다</b> (wash the dishes), <b>요리를 하다</b> (cook), <b>쓰레기를 버리다</b> (take out the trash). Housework as a whole is <b>집안일</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">청소를 <b>해요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I clean. (청소를 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">빨래를 <b>해요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I do the laundry. (빨래를 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">쓰레기를 <b>버려요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I take out the trash. (쓰레기를 버리다)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Why don't we divide the housework and do it?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do idols offer to share chores without sounding bossy? They use a soft suggestion ending, <b>-는 게 어때?</b>, and split the work first with <b>나눠서</b> (\"divide, then…\").</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-는 게 어때?</b> literally means \"how about doing …?\" — <b>하는 것</b> (doing) shortens to <b>하는 게</b>, then <b>어때?</b> asks \"how is it?\" Put a verb stem before it: <b>하다</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">하는 게 어때?</span> Add <b>나눠서</b> to show you'll split the work first: <b>나누다</b> → <b>나누어서</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">나눠서</span>. So the full line = divide (나눠서) the housework (집안일을) and do it (하는 게 어때?).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">집안일을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">housework <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">집안일 = housework / chores. The marker <b>을</b> marks it as the thing being done. 청소, 빨래, 설거지 are each one job inside 집안일.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">나눠서</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">divide &amp; then <span class=\"t-sub\">(나누다 → 나눠서)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>나누다</b> = to share/divide. The ending <b>-아/어서</b> means \"and then\", so 나눠서 = \"after dividing\". You split the chores first, then do them.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">하는 게 어때?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">why don't (we) do…? <span class=\"t-sub\">(하다 + -는 게 어때)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">하다 → 하는 것 (doing) → 하는 <b>게</b> + 어때? \"how is it?\" = a friendly suggestion: \"how about we…?\"</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-는 게 어때? = \"how about …ing?\"</b> — add it to any verb stem to propose an idea together:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">청소하는 게 어때?</span> (how about cleaning?), <span class=\"pt-ko\">빨래하는 게 어때?</span> (how about laundry?), <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 하는 게 어때?</span> (how about doing it together?). Idols use it before splitting up jobs on chore day.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>교과서 · polite textbook form</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Why don't we divide the housework?\" — soft and neutral, good for anyone.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>실제말 · real casual talk</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">우리 좀 나눠서 하자!</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Let's just divide it up!\" — firmer, used between close friends like the members.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of <b>-는 게 어때?</b> as \"how is the idea of …ing?\" — you're asking, not ordering. Chore day? Try <span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘은 빨래하는 게 어때?</span> or to be extra kind <span class=\"pt-ko\">청소를 도와줄까요?</span> (\"Shall I help you clean?\").\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏠</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">집안일<small>Housework · 청소를 해요, 빨래를 해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_chore.webp\" alt=\"집안일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집안일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">집안일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jibanil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">housework / chores</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_clean.webp\" alt=\"청소\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('청소')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">청소</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">cheongso</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cleaning</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_laundry.webp\" alt=\"빨래\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('빨래')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">빨래</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ppallae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">laundry</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 집안일이 많아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 집안일이 많아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There is a lot of housework today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('청소를 해야 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">청소를 해야 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have to do the cleaning.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('빨래를 같이 할래요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">빨래를 같이 할래요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Do you want to do the laundry together?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏠 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> chores take the object marker with 하다: 청소<b>를</b> 해요, 빨래<b>를</b> 해요. 집안일 is the whole family of chores.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍳</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">부엌과 쓰레기<small>Kitchen &amp; trash · 설거지, 요리, 쓰레기</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_dishes.webp\" alt=\"설거지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('설거지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">설거지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seolgeoji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">washing the dishes</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_cook.webp\" alt=\"요리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">요리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cooking</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_trash.webp\" alt=\"쓰레기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쓰레기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">쓰레기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sseuregi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">trash / garbage</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('설거지는 제가 할게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">설거지는 제가 할게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll do the dishes.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리를 아주 잘해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">요리를 아주 잘해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He) cooks very well.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쓰레기를 버려 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">쓰레기를 버려 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please take out the trash.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍳 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 설거지<b>를</b> 하다 (wash dishes), 요리<b>를</b> 하다 (cook), 쓰레기<b>를</b> 버리다 (take out trash).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🤝</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">나누기와 돕기<small>Sharing &amp; helping · 나눠서 해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_share.webp\" alt=\"나누다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('나누다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">나누다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nanuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to share / divide</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b13_help.webp\" alt=\"돕다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('돕다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">돕다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dopda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to help</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집안일을 나눠서 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">집안일을 나눠서 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We divide the chores, then do them.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서로 도와요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">서로 도와요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We help each other.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('좋은 생각이에요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">좋은 생각이에요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">That's a good idea!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 나누다 = to share/divide, and 돕다 = to help. After dividing, help each other: <b>나눠서</b> 해요 → 서로 <b>도와요</b>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-1] Reading — 집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?</span> What is Jiwoo suggesting?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q1\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Why don't we divide the housework and do it?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Housework is too difficult for me.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I already did all the chores.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I don't like to clean.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?</b> = 집안일(housework) + 나눠서(divide, then) + 하는 게 어때?(how about doing?) = a suggestion to <b class=\"hl\">divide the chores and do them together</b>. Only ① matches the suggestion.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-2] Reading — 빨래하는 게 어때?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 우리 빨래하는 게 어때?</span> What is Yuna doing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q2\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Asking what laundry is.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Saying laundry is boring.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Suggesting they do the laundry.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Asking who did the laundry.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-는 게 어때?</b> is how you make a friendly suggestion. <b class=\"hl\">빨래하는 게 어때?</b> = \"How about we do the laundry?\" — Yuna is <b class=\"hl\">suggesting</b> an activity, not asking a fact about it.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-3] Grammar — 나눠서 해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that fits.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">집안일이 너무 많아요. 우리 같이 ______.</span> Fill in the best suggestion.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q3\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>집안일을 나눠서 해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>청소를 벌써 했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>빨래를 싫어해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>쓰레기를 주문해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To divide the chores and do them together, say <b class=\"hl\">집안일을 나눠서 해요</b> (나누다 → 나눠서 + 해요). ① fits the friendly \"let's share it\" meaning; the others are past, dislike, or a strange verb.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-4] Grammar — 하는 게 어때? form</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to suggest: \"How about doing the dishes?\" Which form of <span class=\"pt-ko\">설거지를 ____ 게 어때?</span> is correct?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q4\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>할게요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>하는<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Before <b class=\"hl\">게 어때?</b> you use the <b>-는</b> modifier: 하다 → <b class=\"hl\">하는 게 어때?</b> So \"how about doing the dishes?\" = <b class=\"hl\">설거지를 하는 게 어때?</b> Only ③ <b class=\"hl\">하는</b> works here.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-5] Translate — share the housework</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate: \"Why don't we divide the housework and do it together?\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q5\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>빨래를 벌써 다 했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>요리를 혼자 할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>청소는 정말 힘들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>집안일을 나눠서 같이 하는 게 어때?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The target = divide(나눠서) + together(같이) + suggest(하는 게 어때?). Only <b class=\"hl\">집안일을 나눠서 같이 하는 게 어때?</b> (④) puts all three pieces in place.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-6] Grammar — 나누다 to 나눠서</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 집안일을 나눠서 해요.</span> What does 나눠서 tell us?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q6\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>He divides the chores first, then does them.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>He does every chore by himself.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>He never does the chores.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>He is doing the dishes right now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">나눠서</b> = 나누다(divide) + <b class=\"hl\">-아/어서</b>(\"and then\"). So <b class=\"hl\">나눠서 해요</b> = \"divide, then do.\" It means the chores are split up first — ① is the match.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-7] Vocabulary — trash word</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which Korean word means \"trash / garbage\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q7\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>설거지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>요리<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>빨래<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>쓰레기<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">쓰레기</b> = trash/garbage. The others are other chores: 설거지 = washing dishes, 요리 = cooking, 빨래 = laundry.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-8] Grammar — chore collocations</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the natural sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which sentence uses the chore word with the correct verb?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q8\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>쓰레기를 요리해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>빨래를 청소해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>설거지를 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>청소를 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Each chore pairs with its own verb: 설거지<b class=\"hl\">를 하다</b> (wash dishes) → <b class=\"hl\">설거지를 해요</b> is natural (③). You don't \"cook\" trash, \"clean\" laundry, or \"eat\" cleaning.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-9] Grammar — make a suggestion</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Use -는 게 어때? to kindly suggest cooking together:</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q9\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>같이 요리해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>같이 요리하는 게 어때?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>요리를 벌써 했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>요리는 힘들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To suggest, put the verb stem 하다 → <b class=\"hl\">요리하는</b> + <b class=\"hl\">게 어때?</b> = <b class=\"hl\">같이 요리하는 게 어때?</b> (\"How about we cook together?\"). ② is the suggestion.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-10] Reading — 샛별의 청소 계획</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what best matches the scene.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 청소를 할게요. 지훈 오빠는 빨래하는 게 어때요?</span> What is Seoyeon doing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b13q10\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>She will clean, and suggests Jihoon do the laundry.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>She is asking Jihoon to teach her laundry.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>She wants Jihoon to clean instead.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>She already finished all the chores.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b13q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Two parts: <b class=\"hl\">저는 청소를 할게요</b> = \"I will clean\", and <b class=\"hl\">빨래하는 게 어때요?</b> = a suggestion that Jihoon do the laundry. Only ① captures both.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Chore Day at the Dorm!</h3>\n    <p>Living together means sharing jobs — and Korean roommates love to use -는 게 어때? to split the work without arguments. You'll hear it everywhere from dorms to fan-meeting prep rooms: someone suggests, everyone picks a task, and the work gets done fast.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next chore day, try offering: \"집안일을 나눠서 하는 게 어때?\" (Why don't we divide the housework?) or help a friend with \"청소를 도와줄까요?\" (Shall I help you clean?) — you'll sound like a caring idol roommate!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 14, "title": "It's my first time going to a jjimjilbang in Korea", "en": "한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요", "theme": "first-time", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 14 · FIRST-TIME</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">14</div><div><h2>It's my first time going to a jjimjilbang in Korea</h2><div class=\"en\">한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요 — First-Time · -(으)ㄴ 적이 없다 + 처음 + -는데</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · FIRST TIME IN KOREA</span>\n      <h3>처음 가는 찜질방! — \"한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요!\"</h3>\n      <p>사비나가 한국에 처음 왔어요. 그런데 아직 <b>찜질방</b>에 가 본 <b>적이 없어요</b>. 멤버들이 말해요. \"찜질방은 처음인데요? 우리가 다 같이 가요! 피로도 풀고 몸도 편안해져요!\" 💙 </p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Sabina came to Korea for the first time. But she has <b>never been</b> to a <b>jjimjilbang</b>. The members say, \"It's your first time at a jjimjilbang? Let's all go together! We can relieve our <b>fatigue</b> and relax our <b>bodies</b>!\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Say you've never done something with -(으)ㄴ 적이 없다!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">♨️</span> Say you have never done something: -(으)ㄴ 적이 없다</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👌</span> 처음 (first time) · -는데 (soft filler before continuing)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">😌</span> Relaxation vocabulary: jjimjilbang, sauna &amp; more</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — First Time at the Jjimjilbang!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 Outside a jjimjilbang in Seoul</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">사비나 씨, 한국에서 찜질방에 가 본 적이 있어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Sabina, have you ever been to a jjimjilbang in Korea?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">아니요, 한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요. 조금 궁금해요! 😊</div><div class=\"gl\">No, it's my first time at a jjimjilbang in Korea. I'm a bit curious!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 더운 사우나가 제일 좋아요. 피로가 확 풀려요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I like the hot sauna best. It melts the fatigue away!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요. 찜질방에서 몸이 편안해져요. 우리 온천에도 가 본 적 있어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Right. In a jjimjilbang your body gets relaxed. Have you ever been to a hot spring?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 마사지도 받아 보고 싶은데요. 재미있겠다! 힘내요, 사비나 씨! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">I want to try a massage too. This will be fun! Let's go, Sabina!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄴ 적이 없다 — \"have never done …\" (no experience)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you have <b>no past experience</b>, use a verb stem + <b>-(으)ㄴ 적이 없다</b> (\"there is no time/moment when I did it\"). 가다 (go) → <b>가 본 적이 없어요</b> \"I've never been.\" 먹다 (eat) → <b>먹어 본 적이 없어요</b> \"I've never eaten (it).\" Add <b>본</b> (\"seen/tried\") for a natural \"I've never tried …\" meaning — perfect for a first-time adventure like a jjimjilbang!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">찜질방에 가 본 적이 없어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I've never been to a jjimjilbang. (가다 → 가 본 적이 없어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">마사지를 받아 본 적이 없어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I've never had a massage. (받다 → 받아 본 적이 없어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국 음식을 먹어 본 적이 없어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I've never tried Korean food. (먹다 → 먹어 본 적이 없어요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">처음 — \"first time / beginning\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>처음</b> = \"the first time.\" You can say <b>처음이에요</b> \"it's my first time\" or use <b>처음 + noun/이다</b> to describe a brand-new experience. 한국에서 <b>처음</b>이에요 = it's my first time in Korea; 찜질방은 <b>처음</b>이에요 = it's my first jjimjilbang. As an adverb it sits before a verb: <b>처음</b> 봐요 \"I see (it) for the first time.\" It's the warm way to share a new adventure!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국에서 찜질방은 처음이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's my first time at a jjimjilbang in Korea. (처음이에요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국에 처음 왔어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I came to Korea for the first time. (처음 + 왔어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">사우나는 처음이라서 궁금해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's my first sauna, so I'm curious. (처음이라서 = because first time)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-는데 — \"well… / you see…\" (soft background &amp; filler)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-(으)ㄴ데</b> (after a noun/adjective it's -인데 / -ㄴ데) to set a soft, polite background before continuing — like saying \"well…\" or \"you see, …\". It makes a sentence sound gentle instead of blunt. 찜질방은 처음<b>인데요</b> = \"Well, it's my first time at a jjimjilbang…\" It's also used to gently lead into a request or a question — idols use it constantly to sound warm and natural.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">찜질방은 처음인데요, 뭘 하면 돼요?</span><span class=\"gl\">It's my first time at a jjimjilbang, so what should I do? (처음인데요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">피곤한데, 좀 쉴까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm a bit tired, shall we rest a little? (피곤하다 → 피곤한데)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 시간이 있는데, 같이 갈까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">I have time today, shall we go together? (있는데)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Well, it's my first time at a jjimjilbang in Korea.\" (gentle &amp; polite)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">When Sabina is new to Korea, how does she share that a place is brand-new to her without sounding blunt? She stacks three friendly tools: <b>처음</b> (\"first time\"), <b>이에요</b> to make it a sentence, and a soft <b>-는데</b> ending so it sounds like she's inviting a conversation — not just stating a fact.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Say a whole new experience has <b>never</b> happened with <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄴ 적이 없다</span>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">찜질방에 가 본 적이 없어요</span> \"I've never been to a jjimjilbang.\" Say it's your <b>first</b> with <span class=\"pt-ko\">처음이에요</span>. And <b>-는데</b> = \"well… / you see…\", the soft filler that makes a sentence gentle: <span class=\"pt-ko\">처음인데요</span> = \"well, it's my first time…\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">한국에서</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">in Korea <span class=\"t-sub\">(place + 에서)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>한국</b> = Korea, <b>에서</b> = \"in / at\". So \"in Korea.\" The place marker <b>에서</b> is where an action happens.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">찜질방은</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">jjimjilbang <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic 은)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">A Korean sauna spa. The topic marker <b>은</b> makes it the thing we're talking about. \"As for the jjimjilbang…\"</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">처음인데요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">first time <span class=\"t-sub\">(처음 + 이다 + -는데 + 요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>처음</b> = first time, <b>이에요</b> → noun form of \"is\", and <b>-는데</b> softens it: \"it's my first time, you see…\" The -는데 makes it gentle and ready for more.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄴ 적이 없다 = \"I have never …\"</b> — to say something is totally new, use verb + <b>아/어 본 적이 없다</b> (\"there's no time I tried it\"):\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">가 본 적이 없어요</span> (never been), <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹어 본 적이 없어요</span> (never tried), <span class=\"pt-ko\">받아 본 적이 없어요</span> (never received). This is THE phrase for first-time experiences in Korea.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>없다 → plain statement</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">찜질방에 가 본 적이 없어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I've never been to a jjimjilbang.\" — a plain fact.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-는데 → soft &amp; inviting</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">찜질방은 처음인데요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Well, it's my first time at a jjimjilbang…\" — gentle, invites a reply.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> want to sound naturally warm about a new experience? Pair <b>처음</b> (first) with a soft <b>-는데</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">처음인데요</span>. For \"never done it,\" reach for <b>가/먹어/받아 본 적이 없어요</b>. Practice on the way in: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 사우나는 처음인데요. 뭘 하면 돼요?</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">♨️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">휴식 장소<small>Relaxation spots · 찜질방에서 몸이 편안해져요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_jjimjilbang.webp\" alt=\"찜질방\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찜질방')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">찜질방</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jjimjilbang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Korean sauna spa / jjimjilbang</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_sauna.webp\" alt=\"사우나\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사우나')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사우나</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sauna</div><div class=\"vw-en\">sauna</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_hotspring.webp\" alt=\"온천\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('온천')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">온천</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">oncheon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hot spring</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찜질방에 가 본 적이 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">찜질방에 가 본 적이 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Have you ever been to a jjimjilbang?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여기 사우나는 정말 더워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">여기 사우나는 정말 더워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The sauna here is really hot.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('온천에 가면 몸이 편안해져요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">온천에 가면 몸이 편안해져요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">If you go to a hot spring, your body gets relaxed.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">♨️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> Places like 찜질방 · 사우나 · 온천 take <b>에 가다</b> \"go to\": 찜질방<b>에</b> 가요. To say you've never gone, add 본 적이 없어요: 가 본 적이 없어요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">😌</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">몸과 마음<small>Body &amp; feelings · 피로가 풀려요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_body.webp\" alt=\"몸\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('몸')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">몸</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mom</div><div class=\"vw-en\">body</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_fatigue.webp\" alt=\"피로\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('피로')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">피로</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">piro</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fatigue / tiredness</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_comfy.webp\" alt=\"편안하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('편안하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">편안하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">pyeonanhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be comfortable / relaxed</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('몸이 좀 피곤해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">몸이 좀 피곤해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My body is a little tired.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찜질방에 가면 피로가 풀려요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">찜질방에 가면 피로가 풀려요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">If you go to a jjimjilbang, your fatigue goes away.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여기 앉으니까 정말 편안해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">여기 앉으니까 정말 편안해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Sitting here, I feel really comfortable.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">😌 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 몸(noun \"body\") takes <b>이/가</b>: 몸<b>이</b> 편안해요. 피로(noun \"fatigue\") <b>가</b> 풀려요 = \"fatigue is released.\" 편안하다 is an adjective \"comfortable\": 몸이 편안해요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌱</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">처음과 서비스<small>First time &amp; service · 처음이에요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_first.webp\" alt=\"처음\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('처음')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">처음</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">cheoeum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">first time / beginning</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b14_massage.webp\" alt=\"마사지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('마사지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">마사지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">masaji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">massage</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국에서 온천은 처음이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">한국에서 온천은 처음이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's my first hot spring in Korea.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('마사지를 받아 본 적이 없어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">마사지를 받아 본 적이 없어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I've never had a massage.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('처음이라서 조금 긴장돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">처음이라서 조금 긴장돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Because it's my first time, I'm a little nervous.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌱 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 처음(「first time」) works with 이다: 처음<b>이에요</b>. 마사지(「massage」) goes with <b>받다</b> \"receive\": 마사지를 받아요. 받아 본 적이 없어요 = \"never had one.\"</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Reading — 가 본 적이 없어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 찜질방에 가 본 적이 없어요.</span> What is Yuna saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I've never been to a jjimjilbang.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I'm going to a jjimjilbang now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I go to a jjimjilbang every day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I don't like jjimjilbang.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ 적이 없다</b> = \"there is no time when I did it,\" so <b class=\"hl\">가 본 적이 없어요</b> = \"I've never been.\" It is about no experience, not the present, habit, or preference — only ① matches.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Reading — 처음인데요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">사비나: 한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요.</span> Sabina says…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It's my first time at a jjimjilbang in Korea.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The jjimjilbang is very expensive in Korea.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I go to a jjimjilbang every week in Korea.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I don't have time for a jjimjilbang today.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">처음</b> = \"first time,\" and <b class=\"hl\">인데요</b> = 이에요 (\"is\") softened with <b class=\"hl\">-는데</b>. So <b class=\"hl\">찜질방은 처음인데요</b> = \"well, it's my first time at a jjimjilbang.\" Only ① fits.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — pick -(으)ㄴ 적이 없다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to say <span class=\"pt-ko\">\"I've never eaten Korean food.\"</span> Which is correct?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 한국 음식을 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 한국 음식을 먹어 본 적이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 한국 음식을 먹어 본 적이 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 한국 음식을 먹고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"Never tried\" = <b class=\"hl\">먹어 본 적이 없어요</b>: 먹다 (eat) + 아/어 본 적이 없다. ① is plain \"I eat,\" ② is \"I have eaten before\" (있어요), ④ is \"I want to eat.\" Only ③ means \"never.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — 처음 (first time)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the word that means <span class=\"pt-ko\">\"first time.\"</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 마지막<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 처음<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 항상<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가끔<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">처음</b> = \"first time / beginning.\" 마지막 = last, 항상 = always, 가끔 = sometimes. In context, <span class=\"pt-ko\">찜질방은 처음이에요</span> = \"it's my first jjimjilbang.\" Only 처음 fits.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — make the sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate \"It's my first time at a sauna in Korea.\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">처음</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 한국에서 사우나는 처음이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 한국에서 사우나가 너무 더워요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 한국에서 사우나에 가고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 한국 사우나는 정말 커요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The target = \"first time\" + <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b>: <b class=\"hl\">사우나는 처음이에요</b>. ② says \"too hot,\" ③ \"want to go,\" ④ \"really big.\" Only ① expresses a first-time experience.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Reading — 피로가 풀려요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 찜질방에 가면 피로가 풀리고 몸이 편안해져요.</span> What does Jihoon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The sauna costs a lot of money.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The jjimjilbang is too far away.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> At a jjimjilbang fatigue goes away and my body relaxes.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I've never been to a jjimjilbang.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">피로가 풀려요</b> = \"fatigue is released / goes away,\" and <b class=\"hl\">몸이 편안해져요</b> = \"the body gets relaxed.\" Together: a jjimjilbang relieves tiredness and relaxes you — ③.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — pick -는데</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You feel a bit tired and want to gently suggest a rest: <span class=\"pt-ko\">피곤한데, 좀 쉴까요?</span> Why is <span class=\"pt-ko\">-는데</span> used?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It makes the sentence a question.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It sounds past tense.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> It adds a soft, polite background: 'well, I'm tired…'<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> It means 'because I'm happy.'<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-는데</b> sets a gentle background before continuing — here \"well, I'm a bit tired… shall we rest?\" It is not a question ending by itself, not past, and has nothing to do with happy. Only ③.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — 본 적이 없어요 (never)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You've never had a massage and want to say so. Pick the correct Korean.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 마사지를 받아 본 적이 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 마사지를 자주 받아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 마사지를 받고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 마사지가 정말 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">받아 본 적이 없어요</b> = 받다 (receive) + 아/어 본 적이 없다 = \"I've never received (one).\" ② is a habit (\"often\"), ③ a wish (\"want to\"), ④ an opinion. Only ① says never.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Grammar — 처음 + verb</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 한국에 ______ 왔어요.</span> Sabina is a first-time visitor. Fill in the blank.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 가끔<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 처음<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 자주<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 마지막<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">As an adverb, <b class=\"hl\">처음</b> sits before the verb: <b class=\"hl\">처음 왔어요</b> = \"came for the first time.\" 가끔 = sometimes, 자주 = often, 마지막 = last. A first-time visitor says 처음.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">Reading — a new experience</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 사우나에 가 본 적이 없는데요, 처음이라서 조금 긴장돼요.</span> What is Seoyeon saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b14q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I go to the sauna every morning.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I've never been to a sauna, and because it's my first time I'm a little nervous.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The sauna is closed today.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I'm a sauna expert and I love it.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b14q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Combine the parts: <b class=\"hl\">가 본 적이 없는데요</b> = \"well, I've never been,\" and <b class=\"hl\">처음이라서 긴장돼요</b> = \"because it's my first time, I'm nervous.\" Only ② matches both.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>A First-Time Trip to the Jjimjilbang!</h3>\n    <p>In Korea, a jjimjilbang is more than a bath — it's a whole sleepover-and-relax culture where friends, families, and even idols go to unwind. When something is brand-new to you, Koreans love to hear 처음이에요 (it's my first time) — it opens the door for them to guide you warmly.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next time you try something new, say: \"한국에서 찜질방은 처음인데요. 뭘 하면 돼요?\" (It's my first time at a jjimjilbang in Korea. What should I do?) — you'll sound as warm as an idol showing a friend around backstage!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 15, "title": "I'd like to order two chickens", "en": "치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요", "theme": "ordering-counting", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 15 · ORDERING &amp; COUNTING</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">15</div><div><h2>I'd like to order two chickens</h2><div class=\"en\">치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요 — Ordering &amp; Counting · -(으)려고 하다 + 마리 + -만</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · LATE-NIGHT CHICKEN</span>\n      <h3>배고픈 연습 후 — \"치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘 밤 <b>샛별</b>은 늦게까지 안무를 연습했어요. 다들 너무 배고파요. 지우가 말해요. \"치킨을 먹고 싶어요! <b>치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.</b> 매운 양념 치킨만 두 마리로 해 주세요!\" 멤버들은 환호해요. \"야호! 우리 집에서 <b>배달</b>로 먹어요!\" 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Tonight <b>SAETBYEOL</b> rehearsed their choreography until late. Everyone is starving. Jiwoo speaks up. \"I want fried chicken! <b>I'd like to order two chickens.</b> Just make it two spicy-sauce chickens!\" The members cheer. \"Yay! Let's eat it <b>delivered</b> at home!\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Say what you intend to do with -(으)려고 하다, count the birds with 마리, and say \"only\" with -만!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍗</span> Order food &amp; say what you intend to do</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🐤</span> -(으)려고 하다 (intend to) · 마리 (animal counter) · -만 (only)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🛵</span> Ordering vocabulary: chicken, sauce, delivery &amp; more</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — Ordering Two Chickens!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 Backstage after a late practice</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 오늘 연습을 너무 많이 했어요. 배가 고파요!</div><div class=\"gl\">We practiced way too much today. I'm so hungry!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요! 저는 치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요. 양념은 매워요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Right! I'd like to order two chickens. Is the sauce spicy?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">조금 매워요. 저는 그냥 치킨 한 마리만 주문할게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">It's a little spicy. I'll just order only one chicken!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 양념이 좋아요! 그런데 배달이 오래 걸려요? 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">I like the sauce! But does delivery take a long time? 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">아니요, 금방 와요! 우리 두 마리를 먹고 힘내요, 샛별! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">No, it comes fast! Let's eat the two and stay strong, SAETBYEOL! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)려고 하다 — \"I intend to / I'm going to…\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-(으)려고 하다</b> to a verb stem to say you <b>intend</b> or <b>plan</b> to do something. After a vowel use <b>-려고 하다</b>, after a consonant use <b>-으려고 하다</b>. 주문하다 (to order) → <b>주문하려고 해요</b> \"I'm going to order.\" 먹다 (to eat) → <b>먹으려고 해요</b> \"I intend to eat.\" It's the polite way to announce your plan, like an idol calling out for late-night chicken!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">치킨을 주문하려고 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm going to order chicken. (주문하다 + -려고 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지금 먹으려고 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I intend to eat right now. (먹다 → 먹으려고)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">배달을 시키려고 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm planning to get delivery. (시키다 + -려고 하다)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">마리 — \"counter for animals &amp; birds\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Use the native-Korean numbers with <b>마리</b> to count animals and birds. <b>한 마리</b> = one (animal), <b>두 마리</b> = two, <b>세 마리</b> = three, <b>네 마리</b> = four. For fried chicken Koreans still count each bird: <b>치킨 두 마리</b> = \"two chickens.\" Put the count before the verb: <b>치킨 두 마리를 주문하다</b> = \"to order two chickens.\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">치킨 두 마리를 주문해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I order two chickens. (두 마리 = two)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">고양이가 한 마리 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There's one cat. (한 마리 = one)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">닭 세 마리가 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There are three chickens. (세 마리 = three)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-만 — \"only / just\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-만</b> to a noun to say <b>\"only\"</b> that thing. 치킨 (chicken) → <b>치킨만</b> \"only chicken,\" 한 마리 (one) → <b>한 마리만</b> \"only one.\" <b>두 마리만 주문해요</b> = \"I order only two.\" It's the friendly way to keep things simple — \"just chicken, just two, please!\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">치킨만 주문해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I order only chicken. (치킨 + -만)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">양념만 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I only eat the sauce. (양념 + -만)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한 마리만 시켜요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I only order one. (한 마리 + -만)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I'd like to order two chickens.\" (a polite plan)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do idols announce what they're about to do mid-chat? They glue the intent ending <b>-(으)려고 하다</b> onto the action verb — and Koreans count each fried chicken with the animal counter <b>마리</b>, then trim it down with <b>-만</b> (\"only\").</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-(으)려고 하다</b> = \"I intend to / I'm going to…\". Add it to a stem after a vowel: 주문하다 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문하려고 해요</span>. To count animals or birds use <b>마리</b>: <b>두 마리</b> = \"two\". And <b>-만</b> after a noun means \"only\". Put it together and you get\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요</span> = \"I'd like to order two chickens.\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">치킨</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">(fried) chicken <span class=\"t-sub\">(the food)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">치킨 is a Korean-loaned word for fried chicken. Add the object marker <b>을/를</b> when ordering it: 치킨<b>을</b>. Here the marker waits at the very end of the full object phrase.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">두 마리를</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">two (birds) <span class=\"t-sub\">(count + counter)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>두</b> = two, <b>마리</b> = the counter for animals/birds. So 두 마리 = \"two (chickens)\". The marker <b>를</b> sits on 마리 and makes the whole phrase the object of 주문하다.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">주문하려고 해요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I intend to order <span class=\"t-sub\">(주문하다 + -려고 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>주문하다</b> = to order. Add <b>-려고 하다</b> (after a vowel) = \"I intend / I'm going to…\". So 주문하려고 해요 = \"I'd like to order.\" For a consonant stem use -으려고: 먹으려고 해요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)려고 하다 = \"I intend to / I'm going to…\"</b> — attach it to a verb stem to announce your plan:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문하려고 해요</span> (I'm going to order), <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹으려고 해요</span> (I intend to eat), <span class=\"pt-ko\">시키려고 해요</span> (I'll get it delivered). Idols say this all the time when deciding where to eat after a show.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-어요 → plain action</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">치킨을 주문해요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I order chicken.\" — just stating what happens.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-려고 하다 → intention</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">치킨을 주문하려고 해요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I'm going to order chicken.\" — a clear plan, not yet done.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> -려고 하다 announces <b>intent</b>; 마리 counts <b>animals</b>; -만 = \"only\". Practice your order: <span class=\"pt-ko\">치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.</span> or keep it simple <span class=\"pt-ko\">치킨만 주문해요!</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍗</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">치킨과 양념<small>Chicken &amp; sauce · 주문하려고 해요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_chicken.webp\" alt=\"치킨\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">치킨</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chikin</div><div class=\"vw-en\">(fried) chicken</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b15_seasoning.webp\" alt=\"양념\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('양념')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">양념</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yangnyeom</div><div class=\"vw-en\">seasoning / sauce</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_spicy.webp\" alt=\"맵다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맵다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맵다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">maepda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be spicy</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'd like to order two chickens.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('양념이 조금 매워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">양념이 조금 매워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The sauce is a little spicy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맵지 않은 치킨을 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">맵지 않은 치킨을 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please give me chicken that isn't spicy.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍗 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 치킨(noun) is ordered with 주문하다: 치킨<b>을</b> 주문해요. 양념 is the sauce, and 맵다 is the adjective \"spicy\": 양념이 맵다.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🐤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">마리 세기<small>Counting animals · 두 마리, 한 마리</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b15_counter.webp\" alt=\"마리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('마리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">마리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mari</div><div class=\"vw-en\">counter for animals</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b15_one.webp\" alt=\"한 마리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한 마리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">한 마리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">han mari</div><div class=\"vw-en\">one (animal)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b15_two.webp\" alt=\"두 마리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('두 마리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">두 마리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">du mari</div><div class=\"vw-en\">two (animals)</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨 한 마리를 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치킨 한 마리를 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please give me one chicken.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('고양이가 두 마리 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">고양이가 두 마리 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There are two cats.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('닭은 마리로 세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">닭은 마리로 세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We count chickens by 마리.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🐤 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 마리 is the counter for animals/birds. Native numbers: 한 마리(1), 두 마리(2), 세 마리(3). Count your chicken before you order!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🛵</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">주문과 배달<small>Order &amp; delivery · 주문해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_order.webp\" alt=\"주문\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주문')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">주문</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jumun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">order</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b15_delivery.webp\" alt=\"배달\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배달')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">배달</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">baedal</div><div class=\"vw-en\">delivery</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주문을 하려고 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">주문을 하려고 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm going to place an order.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배달이 얼마나 걸려요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">배달이 얼마나 걸려요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How long does delivery take?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨만 배달해 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치킨만 배달해 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please deliver only the chicken.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🛵 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 주문(order, noun) → 주문하다 (to order). 배달(delivery) → 배달하다 (to deliver). <b>주문만 하다</b> = only order, no extra.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-1] Reading — 주문하려고 해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요.</span> What is Jiwoo saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q1', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I ordered two chickens yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q1', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I'd like to order two chickens.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q1', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I don't like chicken.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q1', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Delivery was too slow.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)려고 하다</b> = \"I intend / I'm going to…\". <b class=\"hl\">주문하려고 해요</b> = \"I'm going to order.\" Add <b class=\"hl\">두 마리</b> (two, animal counter) → \"I'd like to order two chickens.\" Not past (요), not a dislike, not about delivery time. ✨ Rule: verb stem + <b class=\"hl\">-(으)려고 하다</b> = a plan.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-2] Grammar — 마리 (animal counter)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct counter.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 고양이가 두 ______ 있어요.</span> Which word fits the blank to count animals?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q2', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 명<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q2', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 개<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q2', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 마리<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q2', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 장<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">마리</b> is the counter for animals and birds: <b class=\"hl\">두 마리</b> = \"two (animals)\". 명 counts people, 개 counts things, 장 counts flat things (paper/sheets). For a cat you must say <b class=\"hl\">두 마리</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-3] Reading — 양념이 매워요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 이 치킨은 양념이 조금 매워요.</span> What does Jihoon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q3', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> This chicken's sauce is a little spicy.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q3', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> This chicken is sweet.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q3', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I want more sauce, please.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q3', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The delivery is fast.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">양념</b> = sauce / seasoning, <b class=\"hl\">맵다</b> = spicy (adjective). <b class=\"hl\">양념이 조금 매워요</b> = \"the sauce is a little spicy.\" Sweet is 달다, wanting more is more, and delivery time is not mentioned.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-4] Grammar — -만 (only)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that means \"only\".</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which sentence uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">-만</span> to mean \"only chicken\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q4', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 치킨을 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q4', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 치킨이 맛있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q4', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 치킨이 매워요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q4', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 치킨만 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Attach <b class=\"hl\">-만</b> to a noun to mean \"only\": <b class=\"hl\">치킨만</b> = \"only chicken.\" So <b class=\"hl\">치킨만 먹어요</b> = \"I only eat chicken.\" The others are plain statements without -만.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-5] Grammar — intend to (으려고)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to say \"I'm going to order\" (주문하다 + -려고 하다).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q5', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 주문하고 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q5', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 주문하려고 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q5', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 주문했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q5', 1, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 주문해 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">주문하다 ends in a vowel, so add <b class=\"hl\">-려고 하다</b> → <b class=\"hl\">주문하려고 해요</b> = \"I'm going to order.\" ① is ongoing (하고 있어요), ③ is past (했어요), ④ is a polite request (해 주세요).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-6] Reading — 배달</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 배달이 얼마나 걸려요? 저는 치킨 한 마리만 시킬게요.</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q6', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The chicken is too spicy for delivery.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q6', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I want to eat at the restaurant.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q6', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Two chickens are on the way.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q6', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> How long does delivery take? I'll order only one chicken.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">배달</b> = delivery, <b class=\"hl\">걸려요</b> = takes (time). <b class=\"hl\">한 마리만 시킬게요</b> = \"I'll order only one.\" Only ④ captures both the time question and the -만 \"only one\" idea.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-7] Grammar — count + marker</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word order.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">두 ______ 를 주문했어요.</span> Which completes the sentence with a proper counter phrase?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q7', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 마리가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q7', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 마리만<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q7', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 마리를<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q7', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 마리에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In <b class=\"hl\">두 마리를</b>, the counter phrase ends with the object marker <b class=\"hl\">를</b> because 주문하다 (order) takes an object. So <b class=\"hl\">두 마리를 주문했어요</b> = \"I ordered two.\" -가 marks subject, -만 means only, -에 is location/time.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-8] Reading — 한 마리만</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Hajun ordered.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 저는 매운 치킨 한 마리만 주문했어요.</span> Hajun ordered…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q8', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> only one spicy chicken.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q8', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> three spicy chickens.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q8', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> only a salad.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q8', 0, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> one sweet dessert.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">매운 치킨</b> = spicy chicken, <b class=\"hl\">한 마리만</b> = \"only one\" (counter 마리 + -만). So he ordered <b class=\"hl\">only one spicy chicken</b>. Not three, not a salad, not dessert.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-9] Grammar — make -(으)려고 하다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to say \"I intend to eat\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다</span> (to eat).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q9', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹었어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q9', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹고 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q9', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹을 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q9', 3, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹으려고 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">먹다 ends in a consonant, so use <b class=\"hl\">-으려고 하다</b> → <b class=\"hl\">먹으려고 해요</b> = \"I intend to eat.\" ① is past, ② is progressive, ③ is the -ㄹ 거예요 future (a different way to say future).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-10] Reading — 주문만</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 주문만 할게요. 배달은 지훈 씨가 해 주세요!</span> What does Yuna say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b15q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q10', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I'll cook the chicken myself.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q10', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The delivery is already here.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q10', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I'll only place the order — Jihoon, please do the delivery!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b15q10', 2, this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I don't want any chicken.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b15q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">주문만</b> = \"only the order\" (-만). <b class=\"hl\">배달은 지훈 씨가 해 주세요</b> = \"please do the delivery, Jihoon.\" So she'll only order, and asks Jihoon to handle delivery. Only ③ matches both parts.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Late-Night Chicken Runs with the Group!</h3>\n    <p>After a long practice, Korean idols order fried chicken by the <b>마리</b> — and it almost always comes by <b>배달</b> (delivery). Ordering is the perfect moment to use -(으)려고 하다 to announce your plan, and -만 to keep it simple: just chicken, just two!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Order like an idol and try: \"치킨 두 마리를 주문하려고 해요!\" (I'd like to order two chickens!) or \"저는 양념만 주문할게요!\" (I'll order only the sauce!) — you'll sound like you're calling up a fan-favorite chicken spot after a show!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 16, "title": "Can I try this dress on?", "en": "이 원피스를 입어 봐도 돼요?", "theme": "trying-on", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 16 · TRYING ON</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">16</div><div><h2>Can I try this dress on?</h2><div class=\"en\">이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요? — Clothes &amp; trying on · -아/어 보다 (try) · -아/어도 되요? (permission) · 입다/신다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · STYLING DAY · TRYING ON</span>\n      <h3>새 무대 옷을 고르다 — \"이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b>이 새 무대 옷을 사러 가는 날이에요. 옷 가게에서 지우는 예쁘단 <b>원피스</b>를 보며 물어요. \"이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?\" 멤버들은 <b>탈의실</b>에서 계속 입고 <b>신어</b> 보며 고르는데, 서연은 \"이 옷이 사이즈가 좌 작아요. 그래도 잘 <b>어울려요!</b>\"라고 웃어요. 유나는 오늘도 구두 가게에서 새 <b>신발</b>을 사 보려해요. 유나는 느껐요! 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today <b>SAETBYEOL</b> go shopping for brand-new stage outfits. At the store, Jiwoo spots a pretty <b>one-piece dress</b> and asks the staff: \"May I try this dress on?\" The members keep trying on and putting on outfits in the <b>fitting room</b>. \"This fits a little small, but it still looks great!\" laughs Seoyeon. And Yuna is already eyeing a fresh pair of <b>sneakers</b> at the shoe store next door. So much to try on! 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Ask politely to try things on with -아/어 봐도 되요?</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌍</span> Ask politely to try things on: 입어 봐도 되요?</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👌</span> -아/어 보다 (try) · -아/어도 되요? (permission) · 입다 vs 신다</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👗</span> Clothes, sizes &amp; shopping-for-clothes vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — May I Try This On?</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎬 At the stage-outfit store</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">오늘은 무대에서 입을 옷을 사러 왔어요. 우와, 이 원피스 정말 예보네요! 이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</div><div class=\"gl\">We came to buy outfits to wear on stage. Wow, this dress is so pretty! May I try on this dress?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저도 이 반바지가 마음에 들어요. 탈의실이 어디예요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I like these shorts too. Where is the fitting room?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저기에 있어요. 그런데 사이즈가 괜찮아요? 저 원피스는 좌 작아 보이는데요.</div><div class=\"gl\">It’s over there. But is the size okay? That dress looks a little small to me.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">걱정하지 마요. 작으면 큰 사이즈로 입어 볼게요. 그리고 저 신발을 신어 봐도 되요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Don’t worry. If it’s small, I’ll try a bigger size. And may I try on (put on) those shoes?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">우와, 다들 정말 잘 어울려요! 저도 한번 입어 봐도 되요? 샛별 파이팅 오늘 완성! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Wow, everything really suits you all! Can I try one on too? SAETBYEOL styling is done for today! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 보다 — \"to try doing …\" (입어 보다)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To <b>try</b> doing an action, attach <b>-아/어 보다</b> to the verb stem. 입다 (put on) → stem 입 + 어 보다 = <b>입어 보다</b> \"to try on / try wearing\". 신다 (put on shoes) → <b>신어 보다</b>. It’s perfect in stores — you ask to <b>try</b> clothes before you buy them.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\"><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봐\\ec694.</span><span class=\"gl\">I try on this dress. (입다 → 입어 보다)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">반바지를 입어 봤어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I tried on the shorts. (입어 보다, past)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">신발을 신어 봐요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall I try (put on) the shoes? (신다 → 신어 보다)</span></div></div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어도 되요? — \"may I …?\" (asking permission)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To ask permission — \"is it okay if I …?\" — attach <b>-아/어도 되요?</b> to the verb stem. 입다 → <b>입어도 되요?</b> \"May I put it on?\" 신다 → <b>신어도 되요?</b> Stack it onto 보다 for \"may I try…?\": 입어 봐도 되요? = \"May I try it on?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\"><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 옷을 입어도 되요?</span><span class=\"gl\">May I put these clothes on? (입다 → 입어도 돼요?)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 신발을 신어도 되요?</span><span class=\"gl\">May I put on (try) these shoes? (신다 → 신어도 돼요?)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</span><span class=\"gl\">May I try on this dress? (try + permission)</span></div></div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">입다 / 신다 — \"to put on\" (clothes / shoes)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Korean splits \"wearing\" into two verbs. Use <b>입다</b> for clothes you slip over your body — 원피스 (dress), 반바지 (shorts), 옵 (top). Use <b>신다</b> for things you step into with your feet — shoes and socks. And <b>어울리다</b> means \"to suit / look good on\": 잘 어울려요!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\"><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 원피스를 입어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I wear a dress. (원피스 = 입다)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지훈 씨는 운동화를 신어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Jihoon wears sneakers. (운동화 = 신다)</span></div><div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 옷이 저한테 잘 어울려요.</span><span class=\"gl\">These clothes look good on me. (어울리다)</span></div></div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"May I try this dress on?\" (a polite request at a store)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do idols ask to try on clothes — and stay polite? They stack two endings onto the verb: <b>보다</b> (\"to try / attempt\") plus <b>되요?</b> (asking \"is it okay?\"). And they keep two different \"wear\" verbs straight: <b>입다</b> for clothes and <b>신다</b> for shoes &amp; socks.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-아/어 보다</b> = \"try doing …\". Add <b>-도 되요?</b> and you turn it into a question of permission: <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 봐도 되요?</span> = \"May I try it on?\". Notice how a store visit is full of these soft questions — staff are happy to hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 봐도 되요?</span> (may I try this?), <span class=\"pt-ko\">사이즈가 어떻게 되요?</span> (what size is this?).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">이 원피스를</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">this one-piece dress <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">이 = \"this\" (near the speaker), 원피스 = one-piece dress (loanword \"one-piece\"). The marker <b>를</b> shows it’s the thing you act on.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">입어 봐도</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">try wearing, even if… <span class=\"t-sub\">(입다 → 입어 + 보다 + -도)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>입다</b> = put on clothes. Add <b>어 보다</b> (\"try\") → 입어 보다. Then <b>-도</b> means \"even if\" and sets up the \"is it okay?\" question.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">되요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">is it okay / may I? <span class=\"t-sub\">(되다 + polite)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">되다 = \"to become / be okay\". As a question <b>되요?</b> = \"is it fine?\". So the whole string means literally \"is it okay if I even try wearing this dress?\" = \"May I try it on?\"</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-아/어 보다 = \"to try …\"</b> — put it before a permission ending and you ask politely to test something: <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 봐도 되요?</span> (may I try it on?), <span class=\"pt-ko\">신어 봐도 되요?</span> (may I try on the shoes?), <span class=\"pt-ko\">사 봐도 되요?</span> (may I try buying it?).\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>교과서 → textbook form</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"May I try this dress on?\" — full, polite, with the object &amp; particle.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>실제 말 → real everyday talk</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이거 입어 봐도 되요? / 어, 입어 봐!</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Real Korean drops the noun to 이거 (\"this\"), and friends answer with a quick 입어 봐! (\"go ahead, try it!\").</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> 입다 covers anything you pull onto your <b>body</b> (원피스, 반바지, 옵), while 신다 covers what you <b>step into with your feet</b> (신발, 양말). At the shop, practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">이 원피스 입어 봐도 되요?</span> and <span class=\"pt-ko\">이 신발 신어 봐도 되요?</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 누르면 그림과 함께 공부할 수 있어요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👗</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">옷<small>Clothes · 입어 봐도 되요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_dress.webp\" alt=\"원피스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('원피스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">원피스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">wonpiseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">one-piece dress</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_shorts.webp\" alt=\"반바지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('반바지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">반바지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">banbaji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">shorts</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_size.webp\" alt=\"사이즈\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사이즈')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사이즈</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">saijeu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">size</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">May I try on this dress?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 반바지 사이즈는 어떻게 되어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 반바지 사이즈는 어떻게 되어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What size are these shorts?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사이즈가 맞아요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">사이즈가 맞아요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Does the size fit?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👗 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 원피스 (dress) &amp; 반바지 (shorts) are clothes you <b>입다</b> (wear). 사이즈 (size) goes with <b>맞다</b>: 사이즈가 맞아요 (it fits).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👕</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">입고 신고<small>Wearing things · 입다 vs 신다</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_wear.webp\" alt=\"입다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('입다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">입다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ipda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to wear / put on (clothes)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_puton.webp\" alt=\"신다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('신다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">신다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sinda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to put on (shoes / socks)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_suit.webp\" alt=\"어울리다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어울리다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">어울리다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eoullida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to suit / look good on</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 원피스를 입어 봤어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 원피스를 입어 봤어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I tried on this dress.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 신발을 신어 봐도 되요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 신발을 신어 봐도 되요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">May I try on (put on) these shoes?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 옷이 정말 잘 어울려요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 옷이 정말 잘 어울려요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">These clothes really suit you!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👕 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 입다 = put on clothes that cover your body; 신다 = put on shoes &amp; socks you step into. 어울리다 means \"to look good on\": 잘 어울려요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚪</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">쇼핑하기<small>Shopping for clothes · 탈의실은 어디예요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b16_fittingroom.webp\" alt=\"탈의실\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('탈의실')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">탈의실</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">taruisil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fitting / changing room</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b12_pretty.webp\" alt=\"예쁘다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('예쁘다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">예쁘다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeppeuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be pretty</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('탈의실이 어디예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">탈의실이 어디예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Where is the fitting room?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 옷이 정말 예보요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 옷이 정말 예보요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">These clothes are so pretty!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이거 조금 더 큰 사이즈 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이거 조금 더 큰 사이즈 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Do you have this in a bigger size?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚪 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> At a clothes store you ask for the 탈의실 (fitting room) and call things 예쁘다 (pretty). In casual talk 이거 = \"this thing\": 이거 입어 봐도 되요?</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-1] Reading — 입어 봐도 되요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 이 원피스를 입어 봐도 되요?</span> What is Jiwoo asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> May I try on this dress?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Is this dress expensive?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Do you like this dress?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Where did you buy this dress?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-아/어 봐도 되요?</b> = <b class=\"hl\">보다</b> (\"try\") + <b class=\"hl\">되요?</b> (permission). So <b class=\"hl\">입어 봐도 되요?</b> = \"May I try it on?\" — about trying, not price, taste, or the store. ✨ Rule: verb + 어 보다 + 도 되요? = \"may I try …?\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-2] Grammar — -아/어도 되요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">At the store you want to ask the staff: \"May I try on these <span class=\"pt-ko\">반바지</span>?\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The shorts are too small.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I tried on the shorts yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> May I try on these shorts?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> These shorts are really cheap.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Permission to try = <b class=\"hl\">입어 봐도 되요?</b> = 입다 (put on) + 어 보다 (try) + 도 되요? (may I?). Only ③ is a polite permission question: <b class=\"hl\">이 반바지를 입어 봐도 되요?</b>. The others talk about size, the past, or price.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-3] Grammar — 신어 봐도 되요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate: \"May I try on (put on) these shoes?\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">신다</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I’m putting on these shoes.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I put on these shoes.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I can put on these shoes.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> May I try on (put on) these shoes?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Shoes use <b class=\"hl\">신다</b> → stem 신 + 어 보다 = <b class=\"hl\">신어 보다</b> (\"try on shoes\"). Adding permission gives <b class=\"hl\">신어 봐도 되요?</b>. Only ④ is a permission question — the others are statements or ability.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-4] Grammar — 입다 vs 신다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct verb.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 새 운동화를 ______ 봤어요.</span> She tried on brand-new sneakers.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 입어<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 신어<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 쓰어<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 사서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">운동화 (sneakers) are shoes, and shoes take <b class=\"hl\">신다</b>: 신다 → <b class=\"hl\">신어 봤어요</b> (\"I tried putting them on\"). 입다 is for clothes on your body, 쓰다 is for hats/glasses, 사서 is \"buy and…\". Only 신어 fits shoes.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-5] Reading — 잘 어울려요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 우와, 이 원피스가 정말 잘 어울려요!</span> What does Yuna say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The dress is too small.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> This dress is on sale.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> This dress really suits you!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I already bought this dress.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">어울리다</b> = \"to suit / look good on\". <b class=\"hl\">잘 어울려요!</b> = \"It really suits you! / It looks great on you!\" It’s a compliment about how something fits — not size, price, or shopping history.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-6] Grammar — 입어 봐도 되요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">직원: 도와 드릴까요? 고객: 이 코트를 ______?</span> You politely ask if you may try on a coat.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 입어 봐도 되요?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 입어야 되요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 입을 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 입지 마세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Polite \"may I try it on?\" = <b class=\"hl\">입어 봐도 되요?</b> (try + permission question). ② means \"I have to wear it\", ③ \"I will wear it\", ④ \"please don’t wear it\" — none ask for permission to try.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-7] Reading — 큰 사이즈가 있어요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Hajun wants.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 반바지 사이즈가 너무 작아요. 큰 사이즈로 입어 봐도 되요?</span> What does Hajun want?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He wants to buy the shorts.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He thinks the shorts are too big.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He likes the color of the shorts.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He wants to try on a bigger size.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">First <b class=\"hl\">사이즈가 너무 작아요</b> = \"the size is too small\". Then <b class=\"hl\">큰 사이즈로 입어 봐도 되요?</b> = \"may I try on a bigger size?\" — so he wants to try the <b class=\"hl\">larger</b> shorts, not buy, not complain about big, not talk color.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-8] Grammar — 입어 보다 (past)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 이 원피스를 어제 ______.</span> Yesterday she tried on this dress.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 입어 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 입어 봤어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 입어 볼게요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 입어 봐도 되요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Past of 입어 보다 = <b class=\"hl\">입어 봤어요</b> (어 보다 + 아염어요). \"Yesterday\" needs the past tense. ① is present, ③ is future (\"I will try on\"), ④ is a permission question. Only 입어 봤어요 fits.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-9] Grammar — 신다 (feet)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the item that uses 신다.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which of these is something you <b>신어요</b> (put on for your feet)?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 원피스 (one-piece dress)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 반바지 (shorts)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 운동화 (sneakers)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 코트 (coat)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">신다</b> is for things you step into with your feet — shoes &amp; socks. 운동화 (sneakers) are shoes, so you <b class=\"hl\">신어요</b>. Dresses, shorts, and coats all go on your body and take <b class=\"hl\">입다</b> instead.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[16-10] Reading — 탈의실에서 입어 봤어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 탈의실에서 옷을 입어 봤어요. 그런데 사이즈가 작아요. 큰 사이즈가 있어요?</span> What does Yuna ask?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b16q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Do you have a bigger size?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Can I return this?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Where is the fitting room?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> How much is this?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b16q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Yuna tried the clothes in the <b class=\"hl\">탈의실</b> (fitting room), found the <b class=\"hl\">사이즈가 작아요</b> (size is small), and asks <b class=\"hl\">큰 사이즈가 있어요?</b> = \"do you have a bigger size?\" — not about returns, the room, or the price.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Fitting-Room English? No — Ask in Korean!</h3>\n    <p>K-POP idols live in fitting rooms — stylists hand them one outfit after another to <b>try on</b> before every stage. In Korean stores, the magic phrase is 입어 봐도 되요? (\"may I try it on?\"). Staff will happily point you to the 탈의실 (fitting room), and when something fits, idols love to say 잘 어울려요! (it really suits you!) — just like a stylist approving a stage look.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next time you shop, try: \"이거 입어 봐도 되요?\" (May I try this on?) or — when it’s too small — \"큰 사이즈로 입어 봐도 되요?\" (May I try it in a bigger size?) — you’ll sound like an idol at a fitting!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 17, "title": "I cook when I have time", "en": "저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요", "theme": "when", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 17 · WHEN</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">17</div><div><h2>I cook when I have time</h2><div class=\"en\">저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요 — When · -(으)ㄹ 때 &quot;when&quot; + -면 &quot;if/when&quot;</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · DAY OFF · WHEN / COOKING</span>\n      <h3>요리 파티 — &quot;저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요!&quot;</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b> 멤버들의 쉬는 날이에요. 다 같이 모여서 <b>요리 파티</b>를 해요! 지우는 시간이 있을 때 맛있는 음식을 만들어요. 유나는 배가 고프면 <b>볶음밥</b>을, 지훈은 <b>국</b>을 끓여요. 친구 사비나 씨와 대한 씨도 같이 왔어요. &quot;시간이 있으면 우리 같이 요리해요!&quot; 멤버들은 요리하면서 정말 즐거워요. 💛</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today is <b>SAETBYEOL</b>'s day off, so they gather for a <b>cooking party</b>! Jiwoo makes delicious food when she has time. When Yuna is hungry she makes fried rice, and Jihoon boils soup. Their friends Sabina and Daehan come too. &quot;If we have time, let's all cook together!&quot; Cooking makes the members really happy. 💛</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Tell <b>when</b> you do things with -(으)ㄹ 때 &amp; -면!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🕒</span> Say when you do things with -(으)ㄹ 때 &quot;when&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👌</span> -면 &quot;if / when&quot; + cooking-verb collocations</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍳</span> Cooking words: stir-fry, boil, grill, cut &amp; time</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — Cooking Party!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 In the SAETBYEOL practice-room kitchen</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">오늘은 우리의 쉬는 날이에요! 저는 시간이 있을 때 다 같이 요리해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Today is our day off! When I have time, I cook together with everyone.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 배가 고프면 요리를 해요. 오늘은 볶음밥을 만들고 싶어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I cook when I'm hungry. Today I want to make fried rice!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 시간이 있으면 국을 끓여요. 맛있는 국을 만들면 기분이 좋아요!</div><div class=\"gl\">If I have time, I boil some soup. When I make tasty soup I feel great!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 고기를 구워요. 고기를 잘 자르고 구우면 정말 맛있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I grill meat. If you cut the meat well and grill it, it's really delicious!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 우리 음식이 정말 맛있으면 사진을 찍어요. 다 같이 힘내요, 샛별! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! If our food is really delicious we'll take a photo. Let's all do our best, SAETBYEOL! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 때 — &quot;when / at the time of…&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-(으)ㄹ 때</b> to a verb or adjective stem to say <b>when</b> something happens. After a <b>consonant</b> stem use <b>-을 때</b>, after a <b>vowel</b> stem use <b>-ㄹ 때</b>. 있다 (to have) → <b>시간이 있을 때</b> &quot;when I have time&quot;. 만들다 (to make) → <b>만들 때</b> &quot;when I make&quot;. 고프다 (hungry) → <b>고플 때</b> &quot;when I'm hungry&quot;.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I cook when I have time. (시간이 있다 → 있을 때)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">배가 고플 때 밥을 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">When I'm hungry, I eat. (고프다 → 고플 때)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">친구가 올 때 음식을 만들어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">When my friend comes, I make food. (오다 → 올 때)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-면 — &quot;if / when&quot; (a soft condition)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-면</b> (after a vowel) or <b>-으면</b> (after a consonant) to say <b>if / when</b>. It is a gentle condition: 시간이 있<b>으면</b> 요리해요 = &quot;if I have time, I cook.&quot; 볼<b>으면</b> &quot;if (you) boil&quot;, 가<b>면</b> &quot;if (you) go&quot;, 배가 고프<b>면</b> &quot;if I'm hungry&quot;.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">시간이 있으면 같이 요리해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">If you have time, let's cook together. (있으면)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">바쁘면 나중에 만들어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">If you're busy, make it later. (바쁘다 → 바쁘면)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">매운 음식을 먹으면 물을 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">If you eat spicy food, you drink water. (먹다 → 먹으면)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">cooking-verb collocations — 볶다, 끓이다, 굽다, 자르다</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Korean uses a <b>different verb for each cooking action</b>, and you pair it with the food using 을/를. <b>볶다</b> = stir-fry (볶음밥), <b>끓이다</b> = boil (국, 물), <b>굽다</b> = grill (고기), <b>자르다</b> = cut (채소). The verb matches <b>how</b> you cook the food.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">고기를 구워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I grill the meat. (굽다 → 구워요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">물을 끓여요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I boil the water. (끓이다 → 끓여요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">채소를 잘라요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I cut the vegetables. (자르다 → 잘라요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down &quot;저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요&quot;</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= &quot;I cook when I have time.&quot;</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do idols talk about grabbing free time to cook between schedules? They put the whole &quot;when&quot;-clause before the main action — and Korean orders it as subject, then time condition, then verb: <b>저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      The little word <b>때</b> means &quot;time&quot; — but here it turns a whole verb into a time phrase: <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있을 때</span> = &quot;when I have time&quot;. Attach <b>-을 때</b> after a consonant (있<b>을 때</b>) or <b>-ㄹ 때</b> after a vowel. A close cousin is <b>-면</b> &quot;if / when&quot; — a softer condition: <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있으면 요리해요</span> = &quot;if I have time, I cook.&quot; Put the subject 저는 first and the action 요리해요 last, and you have a whole natural sentence.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">The topic marker <b>는</b> sits after 저 to say &quot;as for me / I&quot;. In spoken Korean idols often drop it: 시간 있을 때 요리해요.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">시간이 있을 때</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">when I have time <span class=\"t-sub\">(time condition)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">시간 = time. <b>이</b> marks 시간 as the subject of 있다 (to have). 있다 → <b>있을 때</b> &quot;when (I) have&quot;. This whole chunk is the &quot;when&quot;.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">요리해요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I cook <span class=\"t-sub\">(요리 + 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">요리 = cooking (noun). Add <b>하다</b> &quot;to do&quot; → <b>요리하다</b> &quot;to cook&quot;. The &quot;when&quot;-clause always comes before this main verb.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">때 names a time; -면 sets a condition.</b> Use <b>-(으)ㄹ 때</b> for &quot;the moment/time when&quot;:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있을 때 요리해요</span> (when I have time). Use <b>-면</b> for &quot;if&quot;:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있으면 요리해요</span> (if I have time). In casual talk they overlap a lot — idols blend both freely between schedules.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-(으)ㄹ 때 → a fixed time</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">시간이 있을 때 요리해요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">&quot;When I have time, I cook.&quot; — points to that time.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-면 → a soft condition</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">시간이 있으면 요리해요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">&quot;If I have time, I cook.&quot; — a gentle if.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think <b>때 = &quot;the clock moment&quot;</b>, <b>면 = &quot;the if&quot;</b>. Cooking practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">배고플 때 요리해요</span> (cook when hungry) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">배고프면 요리해요</span> (if hungry, cook). Add the action word that fits: 볶아요 (stir-fry), 끓여요 (boil), 구워요 (grill), 잘라요 (cut).\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍳</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">요리 동작<small>Cooking actions · 어떻게 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b17_stirfry.webp\" alt=\"볶다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('볶다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">볶다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bokda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to stir-fry</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b17_boil.webp\" alt=\"끓이다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('끓이다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">끓이다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kkeurida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to boil</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b17_grill.webp\" alt=\"굽다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('굽다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">굽다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gupda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to grill</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b17_cut.webp\" alt=\"자르다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('자르다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">자르다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jareuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to cut</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('볶음밥을 볶아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">볶음밥을 볶아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I stir-fry the fried rice.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('국을 끓여요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">국을 끓여요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I boil the soup.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('고기를 구워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">고기를 구워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I grill the meat.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍳 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> each cooking verb picks its food with <b>을/를</b>: 채소를 <b>볶아요</b>, 국을 <b>끓여요</b>, 고기를 <b>구워요</b>, 채소를 <b>잘라요</b>. The verb tells <i>how</i> you cook it.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🥘</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">만들기<small>Making food · 직접 만들어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_cook.webp\" alt=\"요리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">요리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cooking</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a4_make.webp\" alt=\"만들다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만들다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">만들다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mandeulda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to make</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간이 있을 때 직접 요리를 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시간이 있을 때 직접 요리를 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">When I have time, I cook by myself.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맛있는 요리를 만들고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">맛있는 요리를 만들고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to make delicious food.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 볶음밥을 만들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 볶음밥을 만들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Today I'm making fried rice.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🥘 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 요리(noun) + <b>하다</b> = the verb 요리하다 &quot;to cook&quot;. 만들다 = &quot;to make&quot;, and you say <i>what</i> you make with 을/를: <b>요리를 만들어요</b>.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">시간과 결과<small>Time &amp; the result · 언제요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_time.webp\" alt=\"시간\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시간</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">time</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_delicious.webp\" alt=\"맛있다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맛있다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맛있다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">masitda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be delicious</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간이 있을 때 요리해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시간이 있을 때 요리해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I cook when I have time.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간이 없으면 주문해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시간이 없으면 주문해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">If I don't have time, I order out.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 요리 정말 맛있어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 요리 정말 맛있어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This dish is really delicious!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⏰ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 시간 = time — 시간이 있<b>다</b>/없<b>다</b> (have / lack time). Add <b>-(으)ㄹ 때</b>: 시간이 있을 <b>때</b> = &quot;when I have time&quot;. 맛있다 = &quot;delicious&quot; — the happy result!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-1] Reading — 시간이 있을 때 요리해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 시간이 있을 때 요리해요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It is time to cook now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I cook when I have time.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I am too busy to cook.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I cook only after I eat.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 때</b> attaches to <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있다</span> (to have time) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 있을 때</span> = &quot;when I have time&quot;. So the sentence means &quot;I cook when I have time.&quot; It is not about right now, being busy, or after eating.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-2] Reading — 시간이 있으면 같이 요리해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 시간이 있으면 같이 요리해요!</span> What is Yuna saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> We are cooking right now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Cooking is very difficult.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I have no time at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> If you have time, let's cook together!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-면</b> &quot;if&quot; + <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이</span> &quot;together&quot; = <b class=\"hl\">&quot;If you have time, let's cook together!&quot;</b>. ① is present-progressive, ② is an opinion, ③ says the opposite of having time.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-3] Grammar — 배가 고플 때</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to say: &quot;When I'm hungry, I cook.&quot; Fill in <span class=\"pt-ko\">배가 ______ 요리해요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 고플 때<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 고프면<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 고프고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 고픈 때<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">고프다 (hungry) ends in a vowel (고프-), so <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 때</b> takes <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ 때</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">고플 때</span> &quot;when I'm hungry.&quot; ② 고프면 is &quot;if hungry&quot; (a different pattern), ③ means &quot;and hungry&quot;, ④ is not a valid form.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-4] Grammar — 바쁘면 나중에</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: ______, 나중에 만들게요.</span> &quot;If I'm busy, I'll make it later.&quot; Choose the -면 form.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 바빠면<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 바쁘고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 바쁘면<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 바쁜면<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">바쁘다 (busy) has the stem <b>바쁘-</b> ending in a vowel, so the conditional is <b class=\"hl\">-면</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">바쁘면</span> = &quot;if I'm busy.&quot; ① mixes two endings, ② means &quot;and busy&quot;, ④ incorrectly adds 면 to the noun form.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-5] Vocabulary — 굽다 = to grill</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which verb means &quot;<b>to grill</b>&quot; (like meat)?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 끓이다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 굽다<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 자르다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 볶다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">굽다</b> = &quot;to grill&quot; (고기를 구워요). 끓이다 = to boil, 자르다 = to cut, 볶다 = to stir-fry. Each food picks its own cooking verb.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-6] Reading — 저녁에 채소를 볶아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 시간이 있을 때 저녁에 채소를 볶아요.</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She cuts vegetables at noon.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She boils the meat for dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She never cooks dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> When she has time, she stir-fries vegetables for dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Put it together: <b class=\"hl\">시간이 있을 때</b> &quot;when I have time&quot; + <span class=\"pt-ko\">저녁에</span> &quot;at dinner&quot; + <span class=\"pt-ko\">채소를 볶아요</span> &quot;stir-fry vegetables.&quot; Only ④ matches the when + what.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-7] Grammar — 시간이 있을 때 만들어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate: &quot;<b>When I have time, I make food.</b>&quot; using 만들다 and -(으)ㄹ 때.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 시간이 있을 때 음식을 만들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 시간이 없어요. 음식이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 음식을 만들 때 시간이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 음식이 있을 때 만들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Correct: <b class=\"hl\">시간이 있을 때</b> (when I have time) + <b class=\"hl\">음식을 만들어요</b> (I make food). ② is a statement of lacking time, ③ mixes word order oddly, ④ wrongly makes the food the subject of have.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-8] Vocabulary — 국을 끓여요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct verb.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">하준 is cooking <b>국</b> (soup). Which verb does he use? <span class=\"pt-ko\">국을 ______.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 볶아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 구워요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 끓여요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 잘라요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Soup is <b>boiled</b>, so you say <b class=\"hl\">국을 끓여요</b> = &quot;I boil the soup.&quot; 볶아요 = stir-fry, 구워요 = grill, 잘라요 = cut — none fit a soup.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-9] Reading — 주말에 케이크를 만들어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 주말에 시간이 있으면 저는 케이크를 만들어요.</span> What does Hajun say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He makes a cake every single day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> If he has time on the weekend, he makes a cake.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Cakes at the store are expensive.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He does not bake on weekends.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">주말에 시간이 있으면</b> = &quot;if I have time on the weekend&quot; + <span class=\"pt-ko\">케이크를 만들어요</span> &quot;I make a cake.&quot; That is exactly ② — a weekend, time, and making.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-10] Reading — 음식이 정말 맛있으면</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 제가 만든 음식이 정말 맛있으면 기분이 좋아요.</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b17q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She feels bad when the food is delicious.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Delicious food is very hard to make.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She only eats sweet food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b17q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> When the food she makes is really delicious, she feels happy.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b17q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">맛있<b>으면</b></span> = &quot;if it's delicious&quot; and <span class=\"pt-ko\">기분이 좋아요</span> = &quot;I feel good/happy.&quot; The sentence links the tasty result to a happy feeling — only ④ matches.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Cooking Together, K-POP Style!</h3>\n    <p>Idol variety shows love &quot;cook-off&quot; segments — members grab free time between schedules and stir-fry, boil, grill, and cut together. When they ask about time or conditions, you'll hear -(으)ㄹ 때 and -면 everywhere. Try using them and you'll chat about your day like a SAETBYEOL member backstage.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ try saying: &quot;시간이 있을 때 뭐 해요?&quot; (What do you do when you have time?) or invite a friend with &quot;시간이 있으면 같이 요리해요!&quot; (If you have time, let's cook together!) — perfect for a cozy food chat!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 18, "title": "Has it already been a year since your baby was born?", "en": "대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요?", "theme": "duration", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 18 · DURATION</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">18</div><div><h2>Has it already been a year since your baby was born?</h2><div class=\"en\">대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요 — Duration · -(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요 + 벌써 + 태어나다/자라다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · DURATION</span>\n      <h3>대한 씨 딸의 첫 돌 — \"태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐네요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 샛별 멤버들의 친구 <b>대한 씨</b> 딸의 첫 <b>돌잔치</b>예요. 지우가 놀라서 말해요. \"우와, 대한 씨 딸이 <b>태어난 지</b> <b>벌써</b> <b>1년</b>이 됐네요! 시간이 정말 빨라요.\" 멤버들은 아기가 <b>자라는</b> 모습을 보고 감동해요. 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today is the first-birthday party of the baby of <b>Mr. Daehan</b>, a friend of the SAETBYEOL members. Jiwoo exclaims in surprise. \"Wow, it’s <b>already</b> been <b>one year</b> since Mr. Daehan’s daughter was born! Time really flies.\" The members are moved watching the baby <b>grow up</b>. 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Measure time since something with -(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요 &amp; react with 벌써!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌱</span> Talk about life milestones: birth, marriage, graduation</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⏳</span> -(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요 (it’s been … since …) · 벌써 (already)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍼</span> Baby &amp; growing-up words: 태어나다, 자라다 &amp; more</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — A Year Already?</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 Backstage before a show</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">다들 있어요? 우리 친구 대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐대요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Hey everyone? They say it’s already been a year since our friend Mr. Daehan’s daughter was born!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">벌써요? 시간이 정말 빨라요. 아기가 태어난 게 엊그제 같은데… 😭</div><div class=\"gl\">Already? Time really flies. It feels like the baby was just born yesterday… 😭</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요. 아기는 정말 빨리 자라요. 벌써 걷는다고 들었어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Right. Babies really grow up fast. I heard she’s already walking!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 어제 대한 씨를 만났어요. 딸이 아주 예쁘게 자랐대요. 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">I met Mr. Daehan yesterday. They say his daughter has grown up very prettily. 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저도 대한 씨 딸이 보고 싶어요! 태어난 지 일 년 된 아기가 정말 궁금해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I want to see Mr. Daehan’s daughter too! I’m really curious about a baby who is one year old!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요 — \"it’s been … since …\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>-(으)ㄴ 지</b> after a verb stem, then a length of time and <b>됐어요</b> (\"has become\") to say <b>how long it has been since</b> something happened. 태어나다 (to be born) → 태어난 지 + <b>1년이 됐어요</b> = \"it’s been a year since (the baby) was born.\" After a vowel use <b>-ㄴ 지</b> (태어나다 → 태어난 지), after a consonant use <b>-은 지</b> (앉다 → 앉은 지).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아기가 태어난 지 1년이 됐어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It’s been a year since the baby was born. (태어나다 + -ㄴ 지)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국에 온 지 3년이 됐어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It’s been 3 years since I came to Korea.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">결혼한 지 5년이 됐어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It’s been 5 years since (we) got married.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">벌써 — \"already\" (time flew by!)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Stick <b>벌써</b> (\"already\") in front of a time expression to show surprise that time has passed so <b>quickly</b> — or that something is happening <b>sooner than expected</b>. 태어난 지 <b>벌써</b> 1년이 됐어요 = \"it’s <b>already</b> been a year since (the baby) was born!\" 벌써 gives the sentence a warm <i>\"wow, time flew!\"</i> feeling.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아기가 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요!</span><span class=\"gl\">It’s already been a year since the baby was born! (벌써 = already)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">벌써 저녁이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It’s already evening.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">딸이 벌써 다섯 살이 됐어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">My daughter’s already turned five years old.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">태어나다 / 자라다 — \"to be born\" &amp; \"to grow up\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Two key verbs for telling a person’s life story. <b>태어나다</b> = to be born (태어났어요 = was born; 태어난 지 = since (being) born). <b>자라다</b> = to grow up (자라요 = grows; 자랐어요 = grew up). Pair them with this unit’s words: an <b>아기</b> (baby) is born (태어나다), then grows (자라다) over <b>일 년</b> (one year).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 한국에서 태어났어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I was born in Korea. (태어나다 → 태어났어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아기가 정말 빨리 자라요.</span><span class=\"gl\">The baby grows really fast. (자라다 → 자라요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">딸이 건강하게 자랐어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">(My) daughter grew up healthy. (자라다 → 자랐어요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher’s Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Has it already been a year since Mr. Daehan’s daughter was born?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">When an idol learns a friend’s baby is already one year old, how do they say \"time flies\"? They hook the past moment (태어난 지 = \"since (she was) born\") to a clock amount (1년이 됐어요 = \"a year has passed\") — and drop <b>벌써</b> (\"already\") in the middle to add that warm surprise.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      The pattern <b>-(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요</b> measures time <b>since a finished moment</b>. Take 태어나다 (to be born) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">태어난 지</span> = \"since (being) born,\" then say how much time has gone by: <span class=\"pt-ko\">1년이 됐어요</span> = \"one year has become (has passed).\" Add <b>벌써</b> and the phrase feels quick and amazed:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요!</span> = \"It’s already been a year since (she was) born!\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">대한 씨 딸이</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">Mr. Daehan’s daughter <span class=\"t-sub\">(subject)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">대한 = a person’s name; <b>씨</b> = polite title (Mr./Ms.); <b>딸</b> = daughter; the marker <b>이</b> marks the subject. The whole chunk names who the sentence is about.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">태어난 지 벌써</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">already, since (she was) born <span class=\"t-sub\">(time anchor)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>태어나다</b> = to be born; add <b>-ㄴ 지</b> = \"since (that) happened.\" Then <b>벌써</b> = \"already,\" stressing that time really flew by.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">1년이 됐어요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">a year has passed? <span class=\"t-sub\">(result · 됐어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>1년</b> = one year; <b>됐어요</b> (되었다) = \"has become / has passed.\" Put the clock amount right before 됐어요 to state how long it’s been.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄴ 지 … 됐어요 = \"it’s been … since …\"</b> — verb stem + <b>-(으)ㄴ 지</b> (the done moment), then a time + <b>됐어요</b> (the clock):\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">한국에 온 지 벌써 2년이 됐어요.</span> (it’s already been 2 years since I came to Korea), <span class=\"pt-ko\">결혼한 지 3년이 됐어요.</span> (it’s been 3 years since I got married). Use <b>벌써</b> when you’re surprised it went by fast.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>교과서 · textbook (polite)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">아기가 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"It’s already been a year since the baby was born.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>실제말 · real speech (casual)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">애가 태어난 지 벌써 일 년이 됐네!</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"The little one’s already a year old — time flies!\" (애 = baby, casual; 됐네! = soft exclamation)</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of -(으)ㄴ 지 as \"since (that past moment)\" and 됐어요 as \"has become.\" See a baby and a calendar, then try: <span class=\"pt-ko\">아기가 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요!</span> — or about yourself <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 한국어를 배운 지 1년이 됐어요.</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌱</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">인생의 순간<small>Life milestones · 태어나고, 결혼하고, 졸업해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_born.webp\" alt=\"태어나다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('태어나다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">태어나다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">taeeonada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be born</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_marriage.webp\" alt=\"결혼\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('결혼')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">결혼</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyeolhon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">marriage</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_graduate.webp\" alt=\"졸업\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('졸업')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">졸업</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">joreop</div><div class=\"vw-en\">graduation</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you’ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아기가 태어났어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아기가 태어났어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The baby was born.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 작년에 결혼했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 작년에 결혼했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I got married last year.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 대학교를 졸업했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 대학교를 졸업했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I graduated from university.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌱 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 태어나다/결혼하다/졸업하다 are life-milestone verbs, often used with <b>-았/었어요</b> (past: 태어났어요, 결혼했어요, 졸업했어요) or with <b>-(으)ㄴ 지</b> to say “since” that milestone happened.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍼</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">아이와 성장<small>Baby &amp; growing up · 아기가 자라요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_baby.webp\" alt=\"아기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">agi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">baby</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_grow.webp\" alt=\"자라다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('자라다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">자라다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jarada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to grow up</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_oneyear.webp\" alt=\"일 년\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일 년')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">일 년</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">il nyeon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">one year</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you’ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아기가 태어난 지 일 년이 됐어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아기가 태어난 지 일 년이 됐어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It’s been a year since the baby was born.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아이들은 정말 빨리 자라요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아이들은 정말 빨리 자라요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Children grow up really fast.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('벌써 일 년이 지났어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">벌써 일 년이 지났어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">A year has already passed.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍼 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 아기 = baby (아이 = child). 자라다 = to grow up. With time + <b>이/가 됐어요</b> after <b>-ㄴ 지</b>: 일 년<b>이</b> 됐어요 = “a year has gone by.”</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏳</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">세월<small>The passing of time · 벌써 시간이…</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b18_already.webp\" alt=\"벌써\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('벌써')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">벌써</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">beolsseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">already</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a8_meet.webp\" alt=\"만나다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만나다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">만나다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mannada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to meet</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you’ll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('벌써 1년이 됐네요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">벌써 1년이 됐네요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It’s already been a year!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('벌써 다섯 시예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">벌써 다섯 시예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It’s already five o’clock.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('대한 씨를 만난 지 벌써 10년이 됐어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">대한 씨를 만난 지 벌써 10년이 됐어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It’s already been 10 years since I met Mr. Daehan.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⏳ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 벌써 adds surprise that time flew. 만나다 = to meet; 만난 지 … 됐어요 = “since (we) met.” Time words + 벌써 is a warm, common way to sigh at the clock.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-1] Reading — 태어난 지 1년이 됐어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 대한 씨 딸이 태어난 지 1년이 됐어요.</span> What does Yuna say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q1\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It’s been a year since Mr. Daehan’s daughter was born.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Mr. Daehan’s daughter will be born in a year.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Mr. Daehan’s daughter was born just yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Mr. Daehan himself is one year old.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">태어난 지</b> = 태어나다 (to be born) + <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ 지</b> = \"since (being) born,\" and <b class=\"hl\">1년이 됐어요</b> = \"a year has passed.\" Together: <b class=\"hl\">\"it’s been a year since she was born.\"</b> It is not about the future, not a recent birth, and 대한 씨 is the father, not the baby. ✨ Rule: verb + <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ 지</b> + time + 됐어요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-2] Grammar — make 태어난</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">아기가 ______ 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요.</span> Choose the correct form of 태어나다 (to be born) before 지.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q2\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 태어나서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 태어난<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 태어났어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 태어나고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄴ 지</b> takes the past-adnominal form on the verb stem. 태어나다 ends in the vowel ㅏ, so it becomes <b class=\"hl\">태어난 지</b>. <b>태어나서</b> = \"and then (born)\", <b>태어났어요</b> = a finished sentence, <b>태어나고</b> = \"and (born)\" — none form the \"since …\" pattern.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-3] Reading — 벌써 1년이 됐네요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Jiwoo feels with 벌써.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 아기가 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐네요!</span> What does Jiwoo feel?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q3\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The baby will be born soon.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The year has passed very slowly.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> A year has ALREADY gone by — time flew!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She wants the baby to grow up slower.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">벌써</b> = \"already.\" It sits before the time and shows the speaker is surprised it went by so <b class=\"hl\">fast</b>. The ending <b class=\"hl\">-됐네요</b> adds a soft \"oh!\" — so the feeling is \"a year has already passed, time flew!\" Not the future, not slow, not a wish.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-4] Grammar — 벌써 (already)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">한국에 온 지 ______ 3년이 됐어요.</span> The speaker is surprised time flew by so fast. Choose the best word.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q4\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 아직 (not yet)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 나중에 (later)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 조금 (a little)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 벌써 (already)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">For \"wow, time flew,\" Koreans use <b class=\"hl\">벌써</b> (\"already\"): <b class=\"hl\">한국에 온 지 벌써 3년이 됐어요</b> = \"it’s already been 3 years since I came to Korea.\" <b>아직</b> = not yet (opposite), <b>나중에</b> = later, <b>조금</b> = a little — none fit the surprise of passing time.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-5] Grammar — 결혼한 지</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate \"It’s been 3 years since (we) got married.\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄴ 지</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q5\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 결혼한 지 3년이 됐어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 결혼하고 3년이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 결혼한 지 3년을 살아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 결혼할 지 3년이 됐어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">결혼하다 (to get married) → <b class=\"hl\">결혼한 지</b> (\"since (we) got married\") + <b class=\"hl\">3년이 됐어요</b> (\"3 years have passed\") = correct. ② is awkward (\"it’s 3 years and…\"), ③ says \"live 3 years\", ④ uses the future <b>결혼할</b> instead of the past <b>결혼한</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-6] Reading — 아기가 자라요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 대한 씨 아기가 정말 빨리 자라요!</span> What does Hajun say about the baby?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q6\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The baby is sick.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The baby cries a lot.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The baby grows up really fast.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The baby is already married.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">자라다</b> = \"to grow up.\" <b class=\"hl\">자라요</b> = \"grows / is growing up.\" With <b class=\"hl\">빨리</b> (fast) it means \"grows up really fast.\" Sickness, crying, and marriage have nothing to do with the verb here — only growing.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-7] Reading — 졸업한 친구</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 졸업한 친구를 만났어요.</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q7\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She met her teacher.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She met a friend who graduated.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She married a friend.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She saw a newborn baby.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">졸업한</b> = 졸업하다 (to graduate) + <b class=\"hl\">-ㄴ</b> = \"(a friend) who graduated.\" <b class=\"hl\">친구를 만났어요</b> = \"met (a) friend.\" The whole sentence: \"I met a friend who graduated.\" No teacher, no marriage, no baby involved.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-8] Reading — 온 지 벌써 5년</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 한국에 온 지 벌써 5년이 됐어요. 서울에서 친구를 많이 만났어요.</span> What does Jihoon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q8\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Jihoon has been in Korea for five months.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Jihoon will move to Korea in five years.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Jihoon left Korea five years ago.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Jihoon has been in Korea for 5 years and has met many friends.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Put it together: <b class=\"hl\">한국에 온 지 벌써 5년이 됐어요</b> = \"it’s already been 5 years since (he) came to Korea,\" and <b class=\"hl\">서울에서 친구를 많이 만났어요</b> = \"(he) met many friends in Seoul.\" Only ④ matches both parts. ① changes 5년 to months, ② is the future, ③ says he left.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-9] Grammar — make 만난</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">우리 처음 ______ 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요.</span> Choose the correct form of 만나다 (to meet) before 지.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q9\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 만난<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 만나는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 만나러<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 만나야<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">만나다 ends in the vowel ㅏ, so it takes <b class=\"hl\">-ㄴ 지</b>: <b class=\"hl\">만난 지</b> = \"since (we) met.\" <b>만나는</b> = \"(who) meets\" (present), <b>만나러</b> = \"in order to meet,\" <b>만나야</b> = \"must meet\" — none make the \"since …\" pattern.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-10] Reading — 태어난 지 1년, 예쁘게 자랐어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 아기가 태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요. 정말 예쁘게 자랐어요.</span> What does Yuna say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b18q10\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The baby was born today.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It’s already been a year since the baby was born, and she has grown up beautifully.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The baby got married last year.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b18q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The baby is sad because she is tired.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b18q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Combine the pieces: <b class=\"hl\">태어난 지 벌써 1년이 됐어요</b> = \"it’s already been a year since the baby was born,\" and <b class=\"hl\">정말 예쁘게 자랐어요</b> = \"(she) has grown up really beautifully.\" Both halves match only ② — the baby is one, growing nicely, not new-born, married, or sad.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Time Flies on the Anniversary!</h3>\n    <p>Koreans love marking time — a baby’s first birthday (돌잔치), an idol group’s debut anniversary, or \"years since we first met.\" When a moment suddenly flies by, people sigh with <b>벌써 … 됐어요!</b> Counting the days since something happened is warm, friendly small talk between fans and friends alike.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Look at a photo and try: \"우리가 처음 만난 지 벌써 1년이 됐네요!\" (It’s already been a year since we first met!) — or about a little one: \"이 아기가 태어난 지 벌써 일 년이 됐어요!\" (This baby was born a whole year ago!) — you’ll sound like an idol celebrating a milestone!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 19, "title": "Maybe I should move near the school, too", "en": "저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요", "theme": "uncertain-plan", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 19 · MOVING CLOSER</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">19</div><div><h2>Maybe I should move near the school, too</h2><div class=\"en\">저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요 — Uncertain Plans · -(으)ㄹ까 봐(요) \"maybe I should…\" + 근처로 이사하다 + 편하다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · A CLOSER HOME</span>\n      <h3>학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요 — \"저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b>이 연습을 마친 날이에요. 지우 씨는 집에서 <b>학교</b>까지 가는 <b>시간</b>이 너무 길어서 힘들어요. 그래서 지우 씨가 고민하며 말해요. \"저도 학교 <b>근처</b>로 <b>이사</b>할까 봐요. 그러면 <b>교통</b>도 <b>편</b>하고 통학 시간이 짧아질 거예요!\" 다른 멤버들도 편한 <b>집</b>을 <b>찾</b>을까 봐요. 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today <b>SAETBYEOL</b> finishes practice. Jiu is tired because it takes so long to get from home to <b>school</b>. So she wonders out loud. \"Maybe I should <b>move</b> to near the school, too. Then the <b>transport</b> will be <b>convenient</b> and my commute will be shorter!\" The other members also think about <b>finding</b> a <b>comfortable home</b> near school. 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Share an unsure plan softly with -(으)ㄹ까 봐요!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤔</span> Talk about a plan you are not sure about yet</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚚</span> -(으)ㄹ까 봐(요) \"maybe I should…\" · 근처로 이사하다 · 편하다</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏠</span> Places &amp; home, living &amp; getting around, time &amp; searching</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — Should We Move Closer?</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 After dance practice</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">아이고, 오늘도 집에 가는 시간이 너무 길었어요. 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Oh my, going home took so long again today. Maybe I should move near the school.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저도요! 이 근처는 교통이 편해서 아침에도 늦지 않아요. 😊</div><div class=\"gl\">Me too! Transport here is convenient, so I'm not even late in the morning. 😊</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">그럼 우리 같이 집을 찾을까 봐요. 편한 곳으로 이사하고 싶어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Then maybe we should look for a home together. I'd like to move to a comfortable place.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">찾다 보면 시간이 걸려요. 그래도 학교 근처면 생활이 정말 편할 거예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Finding one takes time though. Still, living near school would be really convenient!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요. 같이 새 집을 보러 가요! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Sounds good! Maybe I'll move near school too. Let's go look at new homes together! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐(요) — \"Maybe I should… / I'm thinking of…\" (an unsure plan)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-(으)ㄹ까 봐(요)</b> to a verb stem to share something you are <i>thinking about doing</i> but haven't decided yet — like a soft inner \"<b>maybe I should…</b>\". After a vowel use <b>-ㄹ까 봐요</b>: 이사하<b>다</b> → <b>이사할까 봐요</b> \"maybe I should move\". After a consonant use <b>-을까 봐요</b>: 찾<b>다</b> → <b>찾을까 봐요</b> \"maybe I should look for…\". It sounds thoughtful, not decided.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Maybe I should move near the school. (이사하다 → 이사할까 봐요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">집을 찾을까 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Maybe I should look for a home. (찾다 → 찾을까 봐요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">시간이 있으면 우리 같이 갈까 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">If I have time, maybe I should go with you. (가다 → 갈까 봐요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">place + (으)로 — \"(move) to / toward\" · 이사하다 \"to move house\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say where you are moving <b>to</b>, add <b>-로/으로</b> to a place noun. After a vowel or ㄹ use <b>-로</b>, after other consonants use <b>-으로</b>. <b>근처</b>(nearby) + 로 → <b>근처로</b> \"to the nearby area\"; 학교 근처로 = \"to near the school\". <b>이사하다</b> = to move house, so <b>학교 근처로 이사하다</b> = \"to move to near the school\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Maybe I should move to near the school, too. (근처로 이사하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">편한 곳으로 이사하고 싶어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to move to a convenient place. (곳으로)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지훈 씨는 서울로 이사했어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Jihoon moved to Seoul. (서울로, direction)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">편하다 — \"to be convenient / comfortable (to live)\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>편하다</b> is an adjective for places, transport, or everyday life that feel easy and comfortable. Collocations: <b>교통이 편해요</b> (transport is convenient), <b>생활이 편해요</b> (life is easy / comfortable), <b>편한 곳</b> (a convenient place). The opposite is <b>불편하다</b> \"inconvenient\". If you move near school, commuting gets convenient: 학교 근처로 이사하면 통학이 편해요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 집은 생활이 편해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">This home is comfortable to live in. (생활이 편하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">학교 근처는 교통이 편해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Transport near the school is convenient. (교통이 편하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 편한 집을 찾을까 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Maybe I should look for a convenient home. (편한 집)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Maybe I should move to near the school, too.\" (a soft, unsure plan)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Idols rarely announce a big life change like moving in a hard \"I will do it\" way — they soften it into a thought. Instead of deciding, they say <b>-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b> = \"maybe I should…\", the way you talk to yourself when weighing a plan.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b> attaches to a verb stem and turns the verb into a gentle plan you haven't committed to. Vowel stem 이사하<b>다</b> + <b>-ㄹ까 봐요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">이사할까 봐요</span> \"maybe I should move\". Consonant stem 찾<b>다</b> + <b>-을까 봐요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">찾을까 봐요</span> \"maybe I should look for\". Put the place first with the direction <b>-로</b> — <span class=\"pt-ko\">학교 근처로</span> — and you get\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요</span> = \"Maybe I should move to near the school.\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저도</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">me too <span class=\"t-sub\">(also)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = polite \"I / me\", 도 = \"also / too\". So <b>저도</b> = \"me too\" — Jiwoo is joining the same plan as the others.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">학교 근처로</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to near the school <span class=\"t-sub\">(place + direction)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">학교 = school, 근처 = nearby / vicinity. The marker <b>-로</b> = \"(moving) to / toward\": 학교 근처로 = \"to near the school\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">이사할까 봐요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">maybe I should move <span class=\"t-sub\">(이사하다 + -(으)ㄹ까 봐요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">이사하다 = \"to move house\". Add <b>-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b> for a soft, not-yet-decided \"maybe I should…\". It is a thought, not a promise.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐(요) = \"I'm thinking… maybe I should…\"</b> — use it when a plan is still floating in your head:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">집을 찾을까 봐요</span> (maybe I should look for a home), <span class=\"pt-ko\">편한 곳으로 이사할까 봐요</span> (maybe I should move to a convenient place). It sounds warm and thoughtful — idols use it when chatting about future plans before a comeback.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Already decided (교과서)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 학교 근처로 이사할 생각이에요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I plan to move near the school.\" — a decided plan.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Still thinking (실제말)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Maybe I should move near the school.\" — an open, unsure thought.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of -(으)ㄹ까 봐(요) as carrying a \"…?\" to yourself — you're wondering about doing it, not announcing it. Next time you mull a small plan, practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저도 이 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span> or when choosing food <span class=\"pt-ko\">김치찌개를 먹을까 봐요.</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏠</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">장소와 집<small>Places &amp; home · 우리 집은 어디 있어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_home.webp\" alt=\"집\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">집</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jip</div><div class=\"vw-en\">home</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_school.webp\" alt=\"학교\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('학교')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">학교</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hakgyo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">school</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b19_nearby.webp\" alt=\"근처\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('근처')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">근처</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geuncheo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">nearby / vicinity</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 집은 학교 근처에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 집은 학교 근처에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This home is near the school.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Maybe I should move near the school.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우리 집은 생활이 아주 편해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">우리 집은 생활이 아주 편해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Living in our home is very convenient.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏠 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 집 &amp; 학교 are places: 집에 있어요, 학교에 가요. <b>근처</b> = \"nearby\", and it takes the location particle <b>-에</b> (근처에 있어요) or the direction <b>-로</b> (근처로 이사해요).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚌</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">생활과 이동<small>Living &amp; getting around · 이 근처는 어때요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_moving.webp\" alt=\"이사\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이사')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이사</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">isa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">moving (house)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_traffic.webp\" alt=\"교통\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('교통')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">교통</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyotong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">transport / traffic</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b19_convenient.webp\" alt=\"편하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('편하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">편하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">pyeonhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be convenient</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 근처는 교통이 아주 편해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 근처는 교통이 아주 편해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Transport in this area is really convenient.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('편한 곳으로 이사하고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">편한 곳으로 이사하고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to move to a convenient place.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이사를 하면 생활이 달라져요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이사를 하면 생활이 달라져요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">When you move, your life changes.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚌 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 이사하다 is the verb form of 이사 (이사를 해요). <b>교통</b> takes the subject <b>이/가</b>: 교통<b>이</b> 편해요. <b>편하다</b> pairs with 교통/생활/집 for \"convenient / comfortable\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">시간과 찾기<small>Time &amp; searching · 편한 집을 찾고 있어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_time.webp\" alt=\"시간\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시간</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">time</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b19_find.webp\" alt=\"찾다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찾다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">찾다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chatda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to find</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('학교까지 가는 시간이 오래 걸려요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">학교까지 가는 시간이 오래 걸려요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It takes a long time to get to school.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지금 시간이 없어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지금 시간이 없어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I don't have time right now.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 편한 집을 찾을까 봐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 편한 집을 찾을까 봐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Maybe I should look for a convenient home.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⏰ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 시간 = time (시간이 걸려요 \"it takes time\", 시간이 없어요). <b>찾다</b> = \"to find\", with an object: 집<b>을</b> 찾다, 열쇠<b>를</b> 찾다.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-1] Reading — 이사할까 봐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span> What does Jiwoo mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q1\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I have already moved near the school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Maybe I should move near the school (I'm thinking about it).<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Moving near school was really inconvenient.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The school is too far to walk to.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b> turns a verb into a soft, not-yet-decided plan: <b class=\"hl\">이사할까 봐요</b> = \"maybe I should move\". So <b class=\"hl\">저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요</b> = \"Maybe I should move near the school, too.\" It is a thought, not an action already done (①), not a complaint (③), and not about walking distance (④). ✨ Rule: verb stem + <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐(요)</b> = \"maybe I should…\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-2] Reading — 교통이 편해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Yuna is saying.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 이 근처는 교통이 편해요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q2\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> This area has convenient transport.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I don't know this area at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The school moved here last year.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> It takes a very long time to get here.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">교통이 편해요</b> = \"transport is convenient\" — 이 근처(로) = \"this area\". <b class=\"hl\">편하다</b> = \"to be convenient / comfortable\". So ① is correct; the others talk about not knowing the area, moving, or taking a long time.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-3] Grammar — choosing -(으)ㄹ까 봐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which Korean sentence has the feeling of \"maybe I should…\"?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">지훈 is still deciding about moving. Pick the sentence with an <b>unsure plan</b>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q3\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 학교 근처로 이사했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 학교 근처로 이사해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 학교 근처로 이사해도 돼요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">이사할까 봐요</b> (③) carries the soft \"maybe I should\" meaning of <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b>. ① is past \"moved\" (이사했어요), ② is a plain habit/statement \"I move\", and ④ means \"I may move (it's allowed)\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-4] Grammar — make -(으)ㄹ까 봐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Change <span class=\"pt-ko\">집을 찾아요</span> into the thoughtful \"maybe I should look for a home.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q4\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 집을 찾아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 집을 찾았어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 집을 찾을 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 집을 찾을까 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">찾다 (to find) has a <b>consonant</b> stem ending 찾, so it takes <b class=\"hl\">-을까 봐요</b> → <b class=\"hl\">찾을까 봐요</b> = \"maybe I should look for\". ① is plain, ② is past, and ③ is a decided future \"I will find\" — only ④ sounds like an unsure plan.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-5] Grammar — translate to Korean</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate: <b>\"Maybe I should move to near the school, too.\"</b> using <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q5\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 학교가 저에게 아주 편해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 학교에 갈 시간이 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 학교 근처에는 교통이 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The target needs three pieces: <b class=\"hl\">저도</b> (me too) + <b class=\"hl\">학교 근처로</b> (to near the school, direction -로) + <b class=\"hl\">이사할까 봐요</b> (maybe I should move). Only <b class=\"hl\">②</b> has all of them.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-6] Grammar — 편하다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Fill in the best word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 학교 근처는 생활이 ______.</span> Life there is convenient and comfortable.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q6\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 편하는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 편한를<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 편해요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 편하게<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">편하다</b> is an adjective meaning \"convenient / comfortable\". The polite present form is <b class=\"hl\">편해요</b>, and the phrase is <b class=\"hl\">생활이 편해요</b> (life is comfortable). ① -는, ② -를, and ④ -게 (adverb) do not finish the sentence correctly.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-7] Reading — 새 집을 찾을까 봐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 새 집을 찾을까 봐요.</span> What is Seoyeon thinking of doing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q7\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> to eat at a new restaurant<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> to look for a new home<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> to buy a new phone<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> to visit the school<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">새 = \"new\", <b class=\"hl\">집</b> = \"home\", and <b class=\"hl\">찾을까 봐요</b> = \"maybe I should find / look for\". Together <b class=\"hl\">새 집을 찾을까 봐요</b> = \"Maybe I should look for a new home.\" (②).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-8] Grammar — make -(으)ㄹ까 봐요 (이사하다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Put <span class=\"pt-ko\">이사하다</span> into the -(으)ㄹ까 봐요 form.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q8\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 이사할까 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 이사으면 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 이사으러까 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 이사해까 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">이사하다 ends in the vowel <b>하</b>, so add <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ까 봐요</b> → <b class=\"hl\">이사할까 봐요</b> \"maybe I should move\". ② ③ ④ are not real verb forms.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-9] Grammar — translate to Korean</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate: <b>\"Living here is very convenient.\"</b></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q9\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 이곳에서 사는 게 아주 편해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 이곳에서 사는 게 아주 빨라요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 이곳으로 이사하고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 이곳은 시간이 오래 걸려요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"Living here\" = <b class=\"hl\">이곳에서 사는 게</b> and \"very convenient\" = <b class=\"hl\">아주 편해요</b>. So <b class=\"hl\">이곳에서 사는 게 아주 편해요</b> = \"Living here is very convenient.\" (①). ② says \"fast\", ③ says \"I want to move here\", ④ says \"it takes a long time\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-10] Reading — 편한 곳으로 이사할까 봐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 교통이 편한 곳으로 이사할까 봐요.</span> What does Yuna mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b19q10\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She already moved to a place near school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She can't find her current home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She is late every day because of traffic.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b19q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She is thinking of moving somewhere with convenient transport.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b19q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Break it down: 교통이 <b class=\"hl\">편한</b> = \"transport-convenient\" (adjective form of 편하다), <b class=\"hl\">곳으로</b> = \"(to) a place\", and <b class=\"hl\">이사할까 봐요</b> = \"maybe I should move\". So she is <b class=\"hl\">thinking of moving somewhere convenient</b> — ④. It is not done (①), lost (②), or about being late (③).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Idols and the \"House Near the Company\"</h3>\n    <p>Many K-pop idols live close to their company or practice studio so they can rehearse late and still get home fast. When a schedule changes, they don't announce a decision — they wonder about it first, exactly like <b>-(으)ㄹ까 봐요</b>. Moving near work or school is also a super common \"life upgrade\" topic Koreans love to chat about with friends.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Practice like an idol planning a change: \"<span class=\"pt-ko\">저도 학교 근처로 이사할까 봐요.</span>\" (Maybe I should move near the school, too.) or \"<span class=\"pt-ko\">교통이 편한 곳을 찾을까 봐요.</span>\" (Maybe I should find a place with convenient transport.) — you'll sound like a star weighing a fresh start!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 20, "title": "I can't make it this Sunday", "en": "이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요", "theme": "uncertainty", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 20 · UNCERTAINTY</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">20</div><div><h2>I can't make it this Sunday</h2><div class=\"en\">이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요 — Uncertainty · -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 \"seems / I think it will\" + 이번 this + softening a refusal</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · FINALE · MAKING PLANS</span>\n      <h3>일요일 약속 — \"이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 월요일이에요. 멤버들은 <b>이번 일요일</b>에 팬들과 같이 밥을 먹고 싶어 해요. 그런데 서연은 <b>이번 주</b>가 아주 <b>바빠요</b>. 서연이 조심스럽게 말해요. \"아… 미안해요. <b>이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</b> 약속이 있어서요.\" 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">It's Monday today. The members want to have a meal with their <b>fans</b> <b>this Sunday</b>. But Seoyeon is very <b>busy</b> <b>this week</b>. She says carefully, \"Ah… sorry. <b>This Sunday seems a bit hard for me.</b> I have an appointment.\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Soften bad news with -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 so nobody gets hurt!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤔</span> Guess &amp; soften — say \"I think / seems like…\"</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔮</span> -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 · 이번 (this) · softening a refusal</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📅</span> Time &amp; plan words: 이번, 다음, 일요일, 약속, 미안하다</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — Planning This Sunday</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 In the practice room, Monday morning</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">이번 일요일에 팬들과 같이 밥을 먹을까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Shall we have a meal with the fans this Sunday?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 그런데 이번 주말에 다 시간이 있어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Sounds good! But does everyone have time this weekend?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 이번 주가 너무 바빠서 좀 어려울 것 같아요. 약속이 있어요… 😅</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm so busy this week, so it seems a bit hard for me. I have an appointment… 😅</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">아, 그래요? 그럼 다음 주는 가능해요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Oh, really? Then is next week possible?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">다음 주에 같이 먹어요! 서연아, 괜찮아요. 약속을 잘 지켜요! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Let's eat together next week! Seoyeon, it's okay. Keep your appointment well! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 — \"seems like / I think it will…\" (guessing)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요</b> to a verb or adjective stem to say what you <b>guess</b> or think. After a <b>consonant</b> stem add <b>-을 것 같아요</b> (어렵다 \"difficult\" → <b>어려울 것 같아요</b> \"seems difficult\"); after a <b>vowel</b> add <b>-ㄹ 것 같아요</b> (오다 \"come\" → <b>올 것 같아요</b> \"I think it'll come\"). It's softer and more polite than a direct -아요 statement.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">This Sunday seems a bit hard. (어렵다 → 어려울)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">내일 비가 올 것 같아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I think it will rain tomorrow. (오다 → 올)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서연 씨는 이번 주에 바쁠 것 같아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Seoyeon seems busy this week.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">이번 — \"this\" (the time right now / coming)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>이번</b> = \"this\" for a time that is now or just ahead of you. <b>이번 주</b> = this week, <b>이번 일요일</b> = this (coming) Sunday, <b>이번에</b> = this time. Its partner word is <b>다음</b> = \"next\": 이번 주 → 다음 주. Easy way to talk about plans.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이번 일요일에 뭐 해요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What are you doing this Sunday?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이번 주가 너무 바빠요.</span><span class=\"gl\">This week is too busy. (이번 주 + busy)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이번에는 같이 영화를 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">This time let's watch a movie together.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Softening a refusal — -겠어요 / -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 (\"sorry, probably not…\")</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">A blunt <b>못 가요</b> \"I can't go\" can sound rude. Koreans soften a \"no\" to a plan with <b>-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요</b> (\"seems like…\") or <b>-겠어요</b> (\"I probably…\"), then give a reason and add <b>미안해요</b> (sorry). <b>좀 어려울 것 같아요</b> = \"it seems a bit hard\" — a warm way to say no.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">미안하지만 이번 주는 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Sorry, but this week seems a bit hard.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 못 갈 것 같아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I don't think I can go today.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약속이 있어서 다음에 꼭 만나요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I have plans, so let's definitely meet next time.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"This Sunday seems a bit hard for me.\" (a soft refusal)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">When an idol is busy and must turn down a fan event, they don't just say \"no\". They guess about it with <b>것 같아요</b>, add <b>좀</b> to soften, and use <b>이번 일요일</b> to name the exact day — so the \"no\" feels gentle and caring.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요</b> is how Koreans share a <b>guess</b>: attach it to a stem and it means \"I think it will / it seems\". 어렵다 (difficult) → 어려울 (difficult, future form) + 것 같아요 = <span class=\"pt-ko\">어려울 것 같아요</span> \"seems it'll be difficult.\" Put <b>이번 일요일</b> (this Sunday) + <b>좀</b> (a bit — a politeness softener) before it and the refusal becomes smooth and warm:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요</span> = \"This Sunday seems a bit hard for me.\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">이번 일요일은</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">this Sunday <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>이번</b> = \"this (coming)\" + <b>일요일</b> = Sunday. The marker <b>은</b> makes the day the topic of the sentence.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">좀</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">a bit / rather <span class=\"t-sub\">(softener)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>좀</b> literally means \"a little\", but before a \"bad\" word it softens it: 좀 어려울 것 같아요 = \"rather hard\", nicer than 어려울 것 같아요 alone.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어려울 것 같아요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">seems it'll be hard <span class=\"t-sub\">(어렵다 + -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">어렵다 (difficult) → 어려울 것 같아요. The <b>것 같아요</b> ending turns a fact into a polite guess — the secret to refusing warmly in Korean.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 = \"it seems / I think it will…\"</b> — after a vowel stem add -ㄹ (올 것 같아요), after a consonant stem add -을 (어려울 것 같아요):\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">어려울 것 같아요</span> (seems hard), <span class=\"pt-ko\">바쁠 것 같아요</span> (seems busy), <span class=\"pt-ko\">가능할 것 같아요</span> (seems possible). Perfect for guessing and for polite \"no\"s.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>교과서 → blunt \"no\"</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이번 일요일에 못 가요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I can't go this Sunday.\" — direct, a little cold.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>실제말 → soft, natural \"no\"</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"This Sunday seems a bit hard for me.\" — gentle, native-sounding.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> consonant stem → <b>-을</b> 것 같아요 (어려울 것 같아요), vowel stem → <b>-ㄹ</b> 것 같아요 (올 것 같아요). To refuse nicely: <b>reason</b> + <b>좀 어려울 것 같아요</b> + <b>미안해요</b> — try it with a friend: <span class=\"pt-ko\">이번에는 좀 어려울 것 같아요. 다음에 꼭 만나요!</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📅</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">날짜<small>Dates &amp; time · 이번 주, 다음 주</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b20_thistime.webp\" alt=\"이번\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이번')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이번</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ibeon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">this (time / week)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_sun.webp\" alt=\"일요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">일요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">iryoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Sunday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b20_next.webp\" alt=\"다음\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('다음')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">다음</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">daeum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">next</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이번 주말에 시간이 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이번 주말에 시간이 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Do you have time this weekend?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이번 일요일에 약속이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이번 일요일에 약속이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have an appointment this Sunday.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('다음 주에 같이 만나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">다음 주에 같이 만나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's meet together next week.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📅 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> <b>이번</b> = the time that is now / coming (이번 주 = this week, 이번 일요일 = this Sunday). Its opposite is <b>다음</b> = next (다음 주 = next week). Day + 요일: 일요일 (Sunday).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">😅</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">일정과 상태<small>Schedule &amp; states · busy, difficult, possible</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_busy.webp\" alt=\"바쁘다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바쁘다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">바쁘다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bappeuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be busy</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b20_difficult.webp\" alt=\"어렵다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어렵다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">어렵다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eoryeopda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be difficult</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b20_possible.webp\" alt=\"가능\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가능')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가능</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ganeung</div><div class=\"vw-en\">possible</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이번 주는 너무 바빠요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이번 주는 너무 바빠요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This week is so busy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Sunday seems a bit hard.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('다음 주에 가능해요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">다음 주에 가능해요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Is next week possible?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">😅 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> <b>바쁘다</b> (busy) &amp; <b>어렵다</b> (difficult) are adjectives → 어려울 <b>것 같아요</b> = \"seems hard.\" <b>가능</b> is a noun \"possible\" → 가능해요 / 가능할 것 같아요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🙏</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">약속과 사과<small>Plans &amp; apologies · 약속, 미안해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a8_promise.webp\" alt=\"약속\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">약속</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yaksok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">appointment / promise</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2b20_sorry.webp\" alt=\"미안하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('미안하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">미안하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mianhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be sorry</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속이 있어서 못 갈 것 같아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">약속이 있어서 못 갈 것 같아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have an appointment, so I think I can't go.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('미안하지만 다음에 꼭 만나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">미안하지만 다음에 꼭 만나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Sorry, but let's definitely meet next time.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속을 잘 지켜요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">약속을 잘 지켜요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Keep your promise well!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🙏 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> <b>약속</b> = appointment/promise → 약속이 있어요 (I have plans). To apologize: <b>미안하다</b> → 미안해요/미안합니다. A soft no = reason + <b>어려울 것 같아요</b> + 미안해요.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-1] Reading — 어려울 것 같아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span> What does Jiwoo mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q1\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I'm free this Sunday, so let's meet.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> This Sunday seems a bit hard for me — I probably can't make it.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Sunday is my favorite day of the week.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I already met you last Sunday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">어려울 것 같아요</b> = 어렵다 (difficult) + <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요</b> (seems). So <b class=\"hl\">\"This Sunday seems a bit hard\"</b> = a polite way of saying he probably can't come. It is about a <i>guess</i> for the coming Sunday — not being free, not a preference, not the past.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-2] Grammar — -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요 form</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 다음에 만날까요? 지우: 이번 주가 너무 바빠서 일요일에 ______.</span> \"It seems difficult\" = 어렵다 + -(으)ㄹ 것 같아요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q2\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 어려워 것 같아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어렵 것 같아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 어려울 것 같아요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 어려웠을 것 같아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">어렵다 ends in the consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㅂ</b> (consonant stem) → add <b class=\"hl\">-을 것 같아요</b>: 어려울 + 것 같아요 = <b class=\"hl\">어려울 것 같아요</b> \"seems difficult.\" ① and ② drop the needed form, ④ is a past-tense guess.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-3] Grammar — 이번 (this week)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Translate using 이번.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate \"This week is really busy.\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">이번</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q3\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 다음 주는 정말 바빠요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어제는 정말 바빴어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 이번 일요일에 만나요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 이번 주는 정말 바빠요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">이번</b> = \"this (coming)\" → <b class=\"hl\">이번 주</b> = this week. Only ④ = <b class=\"hl\">이번 주는 정말 바빠요</b> = \"this week is really busy.\" ① says <i>next</i> week (다음), ② is <i>yesterday</i> (past), ③ is about meeting on Sunday, not \"busy\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-4] Grammar — polite refusal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the most polite, softened refusal.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Your friend asks to meet this Sunday, but you are busy. Which answer sounds most natural and kind?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q4\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 미안하지만 이번 일요일은 좀 어려울 것 같아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 안 돼요! 못 만나요!<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 싫어요. 다른 사람 만나요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 나는 시간 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To refuse politely Koreans <b class=\"hl\">soften</b> it: apologize + <b class=\"hl\">좀 어려울 것 같아요</b> (\"seems a bit hard\") + a reason. Only ① does that. ②④ are blunt, and ③ (싫어요 \"I don't like it\") sounds very rude to a friend's invitation.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-5] Vocabulary — 바쁘다 (busy)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 이번 주가 너무 ______. 저는 다음 주에 시간이 있어요.</span> Which word means \"busy\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q5\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 어려워요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 바빠요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 가능해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 미안해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">바쁘다</b> = \"to be busy\" → 바빠요. So <b class=\"hl\">이번 주가 너무 바빠요</b> = \"this week is so busy.\" ① is \"difficult\" (어렵다), ③ is \"possible\" (가능), ④ is \"sorry\" (미안하다).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-6] Reading — 약속이 있어서 어려울 것 같아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 미안해요. 이번 일요일에 약속이 있어서 좀 어려울 것 같아요.</span> What is Yuna saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q6\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She is free and happy to meet this Sunday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Next week is difficult for her.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She has an appointment this Sunday, so it seems hard to come.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She forgot about the fans.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Yuna gives a reason (<b class=\"hl\">약속이 있어서</b> = because I have an appointment) and softens the \"no\" with <b class=\"hl\">좀 어려울 것 같아요</b> (seems a bit hard). Only ③ combines the appointment + this Sunday + the difficulty. She is NOT free (①), not talking about next week (②), and didn't forget (④).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-7] Grammar — 다음 (next)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You cannot meet this Sunday, so you agree to meet NEXT week. Choose the correct Korean.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q7\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 이번 주에 만나요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 일요일에 약속이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 어제 만났어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 다음 주에 만나요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"Next week\" = <b class=\"hl\">다음 주</b>. Since you agreed to meet next week, <b class=\"hl\">다음 주에 만나요</b> (④) = \"let's meet next week.\" ① says <i>this</i> week, ② is about an appointment on Sunday, ③ is <i>yesterday</i>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-8] Reading — 있을 것 같아요 (uncertainty)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 오늘은 시간이 있을 것 같아요.</span> What does <span class=\"pt-ko\">있을 것 같아요</span> tell you?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q8\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He thinks he will probably have time — not 100% sure.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He definitely has time, no doubt.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He has no time at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He had time yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요</b> always carries a little <b class=\"hl\">uncertainty</b> — it is a guess. So <b class=\"hl\">있을 것 같아요</b> = \"I think there probably will be (time)\", not a 100% fact (②), not the negative (③), and not the past (④).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-9] Vocabulary — 가능 (possible)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Ask a friend: \"Is this Sunday possible for you?\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q9\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 이번 일요일에 미안해요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 이번 일요일에 가능해요?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 이번 일요일이 바빠요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 이번 일요일에 만나면 안 돼요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To ask if a time works, use <b class=\"hl\">가능</b> (possible): <b class=\"hl\">이번 일요일에 가능해요?</b> = \"Is this Sunday possible for you?\" ① uses the apology word (미안하다), ③ is the adjective \"busy\", ④ means \"should we NOT meet?\" — all wrong meanings.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-10] Reading — 다음에 꼭 같이 먹어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 이번에는 좀 어려울 것 같아요. 다음에는 꼭 같이 밥을 먹어요!</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2b20q10\">\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She will definitely come this time.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She does not want to see her friends at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She can't this time, but next time they will definitely eat together.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2b20q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She already ate with them.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2b20q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Seoyeon softens a no for <i>this</i> time (<b class=\"hl\">이번에는 좀 어려울 것 같아요</b>) and then promises for next time (<b class=\"hl\">다음에는 꼭 같이 밥을 먹어요</b> = \"next time let's definitely eat together\"). Only ③ captures both halves.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Turning Down Plans, Idol-Style!</h3>\n    <p>Before a fan event or a schedule change, idols are almost never blunt. When they must say no to a plan, they guess about it with <b>것 같아요</b>, add <b>좀</b>, give a reason, and apologize — so the listener feels understood, not rejected. This is the polite heart of Korean conversation.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next time you can't make it, try: \"미안해요, 이번에는 좀 어려울 것 같아요. 다음에 꼭 같이 만나요!\" (Sorry, this time seems a bit hard. Let's definitely meet next time!) — you'll sound gentle and totally native!</div>\n  </div>"}]}];